IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc-core-bodies`
IMPORT `uc-core-payments`
IMPORT `uc2-domain`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch1-capital`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch2-earned-income`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch2-self-employed`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch2-surplus-and-floor`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch3-unearned-income`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch4-misc`
IMPORT `uc2-part7-benefit-cap`
IMPORT `uc2-sch10-capital-disregards`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Parts 6 and 7 and Schedule 10 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, alone or as one of a couple, asking how their capital and income are
-- counted, how much capital and income they are treated as having, whether the benefit cap applies to them, and what they must
-- do or tell the Secretary of State.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions such a person would ask.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, or a choice from
-- the modules' own lists), builds the record the module's rule expects from them in its WHERE, and calls that rule. A record
-- field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.
--
-- Where the layer asks for less than the modules can take (the modules still decide the general case; NOTES.md, "Seat", lists
-- these again):
--   * a trade, profession or vocation is asked about one at a time (reg 57, reg 77(4)), the assets of reg 57(5) are asked about in
--     a question of their own, and unused business losses are one figure;
--   * a statutory payment that counts as employed earnings (reg 55(4)) is asked as one kind and one amount;
--   * earlier claims since the old award (reg 54A) are asked up to four;
--   * a grace period (reg 82(2)) is asked with one candidate day, and each of its 12 months with its own rate;
--   * the benefit-cap total (reg 80) takes universal credit, housing benefit and three other welfare benefits;
--   * the exemptions of reg 83(1)(b) to (k) are asked one payment at a time: they are alternatives, so asking again for another
--     payment loses nothing.
--
-- Things that other pieces, or other instruments, set are stated by the person: the thresholds of regulation 90 (piece uc4), the
-- nil UC threshold (reg 54A(6): the formula is not in the source text), the hourly rate of the National Minimum Wage (reg 82), the
-- occupation condition (Schedule 3, piece uc3), and what the Secretary of State has decided ("Has the Secretary of State
-- decided ...?"). The questions never guess a judgment that the regulations hand to someone else.


§ `Universal Credit Regulations 2013 -- Parts 6 and 7 and Schedule 10 -- the claimant's questions`


§§ `Part 6, Chapter 1 -- Capital (regulations 46 to 50)`

-- reg 46. A sum is sorted in four steps: a personal possession is not capital; capital payable by instalments is treated
-- as income where what is outstanding plus the rest of your (and your partner's) capital is over 16,000 pounds; a sum paid
-- regularly by reference to a period is income; all other capital counts unless a rule disregards it (Schedule 10, or
-- regulations 75 to 77: see the questions further down).
@export How is a sum I have treated for universal credit: as capital, as income, or not counted (reg 46)?
GIVEN `it is one of my personal possessions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it one of your personal possessions (for example, a car or jewellery you own, rather than money)?
      `it is paid to me regularly for a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid to you regularly, by reference to a period (for example, weekly or monthly)?
      `it is payable to me by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it capital that is payable to you by instalments?
      `the amount of it that is still outstanding` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is payable by instalments, how much of it, in pounds, is still outstanding? (0 if it is not payable by instalments)
      `all my other capital, and my partner's` IS A NUMBER @desc How much other capital, in pounds, do you have, together with your partner's if you have one?
      `a rule leaves this capital out of the count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it capital that a rule leaves out of the count (see the questions about Schedule 10 and about regulations 75 to 77 below)?
GIVETH A `Treatment of a sum under regulation 46`
DECIDE `How is a sum I have treated for universal credit` IS
    `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` `my sum`
    WHERE
        `my sum` MEANS `Sum considered under regulation 46` WITH
            `personal possession` IS `it is one of my personal possessions`
            `sum paid regularly and by reference to a period` IS `it is paid to me regularly for a period`
            `capital payable by instalments` IS `it is payable to me by instalments`
            `amount of the capital outstanding` IS `the amount of it that is still outstanding`
            `other capital of the person and, if the person is a member of a couple, of the other member` IS `all my other capital, and my partner's`
            `capital to be disregarded under regulation 48` IS `a rule leaves this capital out of the count`

-- reg 46(4). Each instalment of capital payable by instalments is treated as income if the outstanding amount plus your other
-- capital is over 16,000 pounds.
@export Is each instalment of capital I am paid by instalments treated as income (reg 46(4))?
GIVEN `the amount of it that is still outstanding` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the capital, in pounds, is still outstanding?
      `all my other capital, and my partner's` IS A NUMBER @desc How much other capital, in pounds, do you have, together with your partner's if you have one?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is each instalment of capital I am paid by instalments treated as income` IF
    `reg 46(4) — each instalment is treated as income` `my sum`
    WHERE
        `my sum` MEANS `Sum considered under regulation 46` WITH
            `amount of the capital outstanding` IS `the amount of it that is still outstanding`
            `other capital of the person and, if the person is a member of a couple, of the other member` IS `all my other capital, and my partner's`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `personal possession` IS FALSE
            `sum paid regularly and by reference to a period` IS FALSE
            `capital payable by instalments` IS FALSE
            `capital to be disregarded under regulation 48` IS FALSE

-- reg 47. Capital you own jointly with others is treated, unless there is evidence to the contrary, as shared equally. The text
-- does not say what share applies when the evidence is to the contrary: you state the share the evidence shows, and the answer is
-- then that share of the whole.
@export How much of a capital asset I own jointly with others is mine, in pounds (reg 47)?
GIVEN `the whole value of what we own together` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value, in pounds, of the whole of what you own together?
      `how many of us own it, including me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people have a beneficial interest in it, counting you?
      `the evidence shows my share is different` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the evidence show that your share is not an equal one?
      `my share according to the evidence` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what fraction of the whole is your share? (for example 0.25 for a quarter; 0 if the evidence does not show a different share)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of a capital asset I own jointly with others is mine` IS
    `reg 47 — the value of the person's share of jointly held capital` `our asset`
    WHERE
        `our asset` MEANS `Jointly held capital asset` WITH
            `value of the whole of the beneficial interest` IS `the whole value of what we own together`
            `number of persons with a beneficial interest, including the person` IS `how many of us own it, including me`
            `fraction of the whole that the evidence to the contrary shows is the person's share` IS IF `the evidence shows my share is different` THEN JUST `my share according to the evidence` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 48(2). Schedule 10 says 6 months in several places. The Secretary of State may extend that where it is reasonable; the text
-- names no limit, and an extension is a judgment, so the length it has been extended to is something you state.
@export How many months does the 6-month period in Schedule 10 last for me (reg 48(2))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State told you that a 6-month period in Schedule 10 is extended in your case?
      `the months it has been extended to` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, to how many months? (0 if it has not been extended)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months does the 6-month period in Schedule 10 last for me` IS
    (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (IF `the Secretary of State has extended the period` THEN JUST `the months it has been extended to` ELSE NOTHING))'s quantity

-- reg 49. The value of capital is its current market value (or surrender value) in the country where you hold it, less 10% if
-- there would be selling expenses, less any encumbrances secured on it; for an asset abroad that cannot be transferred here,
-- what it would raise if sold here; for money held in another currency, after any banking charge for converting it.
@export What is my capital asset worth for universal credit, in pounds (reg 49)?
GIVEN `the market value of the asset` IS A NUMBER @desc What is its current market value or surrender value, in pounds, in the country where you have it?
      `I have it outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have it outside the United Kingdom?
      `I cannot transfer its value to the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are you prohibited, in that country, from transferring an amount equal to its value to the United Kingdom?
      `what it would raise if sold in the United Kingdom` IS A NUMBER @desc What would it raise, in pounds, if sold in the United Kingdom to a willing buyer? (0 if it is not outside the United Kingdom)
      `there would be expenses of selling it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would there be expenses attributable to selling it?
      `what is owed on it` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, is secured on it (for example the balance of a mortgage)?
      `it is held in a currency other than sterling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it held in a currency other than sterling?
      `the charge for converting it into sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What banking charge or commission, in pounds, would be payable in converting it into sterling? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my capital asset worth for universal credit` IS
    `reg 49 — the value of capital` `my asset`
    WHERE
        `my asset` MEANS `Capital asset to be valued` WITH
            `current market value or surrender value of the asset (in the country where it is possessed, in sterling terms)` IS `the market value of the asset`
            `possessed in a country outside the United Kingdom` IS `I have it outside the United Kingdom`
            `prohibition in that country against transferring an amount equal to the value to the United Kingdom` IS `I cannot transfer its value to the United Kingdom`
            `amount it would raise if sold in the United Kingdom to a willing buyer` IS `what it would raise if sold in the United Kingdom`
            `there would be expenses attributable to sale` IS `there would be expenses of selling it`
            `amount of any encumbrances secured on it` IS `what is owed on it`
            `held in a currency other than sterling` IS `it is held in a currency other than sterling`
            `banking charge or commission payable in converting it into sterling` IS `the charge for converting it into sterling`

-- reg 50(1), (2). You are treated as still having capital you deprived yourself of in order to get universal credit or more of it,
-- unless you disposed of it to reduce or pay a debt you owe, or to buy goods or services and the expense was reasonable.
@export Am I treated as still having capital that I got rid of (reg 50(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I got rid of the capital to get universal credit or more of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you get rid of the capital in order to get universal credit, or to get more of it?
      `I used it to reduce or pay a debt I owe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it to reduce or pay a debt that you owe?
      `I used it to buy goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it to buy goods or services?
      `the spending was reasonable for someone in my circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that spending reasonable in your circumstances?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as still having capital that I got rid of` IF
    `reg 50(1) — the person is treated as possessing the capital` `my disposal`
    WHERE
        `my disposal` MEANS `Disposal of capital considered under regulation 50` WITH
            `deprived themselves of the capital for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit` IS `I got rid of the capital to get universal credit or more of it`
            `disposed of it for the purpose of reducing or paying a debt owed by the person` IS `I used it to reduce or pay a debt I owe`
            `disposed of it for the purpose of purchasing goods or services` IS `I used it to buy goods or services`
            `the expenditure was reasonable in the circumstances of the person's case` IS `the spending was reasonable for someone in my circumstances`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `amount of the capital of which the person has deprived themselves` IS 0

-- reg 50(1), (2). How much capital you are treated as still having, in pounds.
@export How much capital that I got rid of am I treated as still having, in pounds (reg 50(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the amount of capital I got rid of` IS A NUMBER @desc How much capital, in pounds, did you get rid of?
      `I got rid of the capital to get universal credit or more of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you get rid of the capital in order to get universal credit, or to get more of it?
      `I used it to reduce or pay a debt I owe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it to reduce or pay a debt that you owe?
      `I used it to buy goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it to buy goods or services?
      `the spending was reasonable for someone in my circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that spending reasonable in your circumstances?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much capital that I got rid of am I treated as still having` IS
    `reg 50(1) — the notional capital` `my disposal`
    WHERE
        `my disposal` MEANS `Disposal of capital considered under regulation 50` WITH
            `amount of the capital of which the person has deprived themselves` IS `the amount of capital I got rid of`
            `deprived themselves of the capital for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit` IS `I got rid of the capital to get universal credit or more of it`
            `disposed of it for the purpose of reducing or paying a debt owed by the person` IS `I used it to reduce or pay a debt I owe`
            `disposed of it for the purpose of purchasing goods or services` IS `I used it to buy goods or services`
            `the expenditure was reasonable in the circumstances of the person's case` IS `the spending was reasonable for someone in my circumstances`

-- reg 50(3). In each later assessment period the notional capital goes down: over 16,000 pounds, by the award the Secretary of State
-- considers you would have had but for it; between 6,000 and 16,000, by the income it is treated as yielding. The amount of the
-- award is the Secretary of State's judgment, so you state it.
@export How much notional capital do I have after an assessment period, in pounds (reg 50(3))?
GIVEN `my notional capital at the start of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much notional capital, in pounds, did you have at the start of the assessment period (or month)?
      `the award I would have had without it` IS A NUMBER @desc What award of universal credit, in pounds, would the Secretary of State consider you would have had, were it not for the notional capital?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much notional capital do I have after an assessment period` IS
    `reg 50(3) — the notional capital after an assessment period or month` `my notional capital at the start of the period` `the award I would have had without it`


§§ `Part 6, Chapter 2 -- Earned income (regulations 52 to 64)`

-- reg 52. Earned income is remuneration or profits from a job, a trade, profession or vocation, or other paid work, and anything
-- this Chapter treats as earned income.
@export Is the income I receive earned income (reg 52)?
GIVEN `it is pay or profit from a job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it remuneration or profit from a job (a contract of service, or an office)?
      `it is profit from my trade, profession or vocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it remuneration or profit from a trade, profession or vocation of yours?
      `it comes from work that I do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it come from work that you do?
      `the work is done for pay or in expectation of pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that work done for payment, or in expectation of payment?
      `I do the work for a charity or voluntary organisation, or as a volunteer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do that work for a charity or voluntary organisation, or as a volunteer?
      `I am paid only my expenses for the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you receive for that work only in respect of your expenses?
      `the Chapter treats it as earned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it income that Chapter 2 of Part 6 of the Regulations treats as earned income (for example, the minimum income floor or surplus earnings)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the income I receive earned income` IF
    `reg 52 — income is earned income` `my income`
    WHERE
        `my income` MEANS `Income considered under regulation 52` WITH
            `remuneration or profits derived from employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office` IS `it is pay or profit from a job`
            `remuneration or profits derived from a trade, profession or vocation` IS `it is profit from my trade, profession or vocation`
            `income derived from work done by the person` IS `it comes from work that I do`
            `work from which the income is derived` IS `the work I do`
            `income treated as earned income in accordance with this Chapter` IS `the Chapter treats it as earned income`
        `the work I do` MEANS `Work done by a person` WITH
            `work is done for payment or in expectation of payment` IS `the work is done for pay or in expectation of pay`
            `person is engaged by a charitable or voluntary organisation, or as a volunteer` IS `I do the work for a charity or voluntary organisation, or as a volunteer`
            `payment received or due to be paid is only in respect of expenses` IS `I am paid only my expenses for the work`

-- reg 53(2). A person participating as a service user (consulted about health, social care, social housing, or social security
-- services) is not treated as having earned income from the payments they receive for it; the Regulations call it "participating as a
-- service user".
@export Am I participating as a service user (reg 53(2))?
GIVEN `I am consulted by or for a body with a duty to provide health, social care or social housing services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing?
      `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors such services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services?
      `I am consulted as a user or potential user of those services, or a carer or person affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted in your capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services?
      `I am consulted by or for the Secretary of State about social security, child support or employment and training functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of the Secretary of State in relation to the Secretary of State's functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973?
      `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors those functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions?
      `I am consulted as a person affected by those functions, or the carer of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted in your capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions, or the carer of such a person?
      `I am the carer of a person who is consulted in that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the carer of a person consulted under the first or the fourth of those questions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I participating as a service user` IF
    `reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` `my participation`
    WHERE
        `my participation` MEANS `Person who may be participating as a service user` WITH
            `consulted by or on behalf of a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing` IS `I am consulted by or for a body with a duty to provide health, social care or social housing services`
            `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services` IS `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors such services`
            `consulted in their capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services` IS `I am consulted as a user or potential user of those services, or a carer or person affected`
            `consulted by or on behalf of the Secretary of State in relation to the Secretary of State's functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973` IS `I am consulted by or for the Secretary of State about social security, child support or employment and training functions`
            `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions` IS `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors those functions`
            `consulted in their capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions or the carer of such a person` IS `I am consulted as a person affected by those functions, or the carer of such a person`
            `the carer of a person consulted under sub-paragraph (a) or (ab)` IS `I am the carer of a person who is consulted in that way`

-- reg 54(2). The Secretary of State may base a determination on an estimate in two cases: a determination made before the first
-- assessment period has ended of whether you meet the financial conditions, or one of your earned income where you have failed to
-- report information about it.
@export May a decision about my earned income be based on an estimate (reg 54(2))?
GIVEN `the decision is about the financial conditions and is made before my first assessment period ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one about whether you meet the financial conditions for universal credit, made before your first assessment period has ended?
      `the decision is about my earned income and I have not reported information about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one about the amount of your earned income for an assessment period, where you have failed to report information about that earned income?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a decision about my earned income be based on an estimate` IF
    `reg 54(2) — the determination may be based on an estimate` `the decision`
    WHERE
        `the decision` MEANS `Determination that may be based on an estimate` WITH
            `determination of whether the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act are met, made before the expiry of the first assessment period in relation to a claim` IS `the decision is about the financial conditions and is made before my first assessment period ends`
            `determination of the amount of the person's earned income for an assessment period, where the person has failed to report information in relation to that earned income` IS `the decision is about my earned income and I have not reported information about it`

-- reg 54(1). Your earned income for an assessment period is based on the amounts you actually received; where an estimate is
-- allowed under reg 54(2) and the Secretary of State has made one, on the estimate.
@export On which amount is my earned income for an assessment period based, in pounds (reg 54(1))?
GIVEN `the decision is about the financial conditions and is made before my first assessment period ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one about whether you meet the financial conditions for universal credit, made before your first assessment period has ended?
      `the decision is about my earned income and I have not reported information about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one about the amount of your earned income for an assessment period, where you have failed to report information about that earned income?
      `what I actually received in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you actually receive in the assessment period?
      `the Secretary of State has made an estimate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State made an estimate of what you received or are expected to receive in the assessment period?
      `the estimate` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what is the estimate, in pounds? (0 if there is none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `On which amount is my earned income for an assessment period based` IS
    `reg 54(1) — the amounts on which the earned income for an assessment period is based` `the decision` `what I actually received in the period` (IF `the Secretary of State has made an estimate` THEN JUST `the estimate` ELSE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        `the decision` MEANS `Determination that may be based on an estimate` WITH
            `determination of whether the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act are met, made before the expiry of the first assessment period in relation to a claim` IS `the decision is about the financial conditions and is made before my first assessment period ends`
            `determination of the amount of the person's earned income for an assessment period, where the person has failed to report information in relation to that earned income` IS `the decision is about my earned income and I have not reported information about it`

-- reg 54A. If your earlier award ended within the last 6 months, you have not been entitled since, and your earned income in the month
-- that would have been the final assessment period was over the relevant threshold, the surplus over the threshold is treated as
-- earned income in your new claim (but not if you are a recent victim of domestic violence). Where you have made earlier claims in the
-- meantime, the surplus is carried through them (at most four earlier claims are provided for). For a first joint claim by a couple
-- who each had an award, the surplus is the sum of what each would have had; for a single claim after a joint one, or the reverse, the
-- Secretary of State apportions it. The seat takes up to four earlier claims; the nil UC threshold is stated, because the text of its
-- formula is not in the source.
@export How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income, in pounds (reg 54A)?
GIVEN `I or my partner had an earlier award of universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, or either of you if you claim jointly, have an earlier award of universal credit (the old award)?
      `the day my earlier award ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the old award end?
      `the first day my new claim is made for` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day for which your new claim is made?
      `neither of us has been entitled since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that neither of you has been entitled to universal credit since the old award ended?
      `earned income in the last month of my earlier award` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your total earned income, in pounds, in the month that would have been the final assessment period for the old award, had it not ended?
      `the nil UC threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nil UC threshold, in pounds (the earned income at which no universal credit is payable)?
      `how many earlier claims I have made since` IS A NUMBER @desc How many earlier claims have you made since the old award ended?
      `earned income in the first month of my first earlier claim` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income, in pounds, in the month that would have been the first assessment period of your first earlier claim? (0 if none)
      `earned income in the first month of my second earlier claim` IS A NUMBER @desc Likewise for your second earlier claim (0 if none)
      `earned income in the first month of my third earlier claim` IS A NUMBER @desc Likewise for your third earlier claim (0 if none)
      `earned income in the first month of my fourth earlier claim` IS A NUMBER @desc Likewise for your fourth earlier claim (0 if none)
      `I have recently been a victim of domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, or did you at the time the old award ended, recently been a victim of domestic violence?
      `this is a first joint claim by two people who each had an award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the first joint claim by two people who each had an old award?
      `my surplus had I claimed alone` IS A NUMBER @desc What surplus earnings, in pounds, would have been treated as your earned income had you claimed as a single person? (0 if not a joint claim)
      `my partner's surplus had they claimed alone` IS A NUMBER @desc What surplus earnings, in pounds, would have been treated as your partner's earned income had they claimed as a single person? (0 if not a joint claim)
      `this is a single claim after a joint one, or a joint one after a different couple's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a single claim after an award or claim as a joint claimant, or a joint claim after an award or claim as a member of a different couple?
      `the Secretary of State has apportioned the surplus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, has the Secretary of State apportioned the surplus to your claim?
      `the portion apportioned to my claim` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what portion of the surplus, in pounds, is apportioned to your claim? (0 if not apportioned)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` IS
    `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` `my claim`
    WHERE
        `my claim` MEANS `Claim considered under regulation 54A` WITH
            `the claimant, or either of joint claimants, had an award of universal credit (the old award)` IS `I or my partner had an earlier award of universal credit`
            `date on which the old award terminated` IS `the day my earlier award ended`
            `first day in respect of which the claim is made` IS `the first day my new claim is made for`
            `the claimant has not, or neither of joint claimants has, been entitled to universal credit since the old award terminated` IS `neither of us has been entitled since`
            `total earned income in the month that would have been the final assessment period for the old award, had it not terminated` IS `earned income in the last month of my earlier award`
            `nil UC threshold` IS `the nil UC threshold`
            `total earned income in the month that would have been the first assessment period in relation to each earlier claim since the old award terminated` IS IF `how many earlier claims I have made since` GREATER THAN 4 THEN LIST 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 ELSE (IF `how many earlier claims I have made since` EQUALS 0 THEN EMPTY ELSE (IF `how many earlier claims I have made since` EQUALS 1 THEN LIST `earned income in the first month of my first earlier claim` ELSE (IF `how many earlier claims I have made since` EQUALS 2 THEN LIST `earned income in the first month of my first earlier claim`, `earned income in the first month of my second earlier claim` ELSE (IF `how many earlier claims I have made since` EQUALS 3 THEN LIST `earned income in the first month of my first earlier claim`, `earned income in the first month of my second earlier claim`, `earned income in the first month of my third earlier claim` ELSE LIST `earned income in the first month of my first earlier claim`, `earned income in the first month of my second earlier claim`, `earned income in the first month of my third earlier claim`, `earned income in the first month of my fourth earlier claim`))))
            `the claimant has, or had at the time the old award terminated, recently been a victim of domestic violence` IS `I have recently been a victim of domestic violence`
            `first joint claim by members of a couple each of whom had an old award` IS `this is a first joint claim by two people who each had an award`
            `surplus earnings of each member of the couple that would have been treated as earned income had they each claimed as a single person` IS LIST `my surplus had I claimed alone`, `my partner's surplus had they claimed alone`
            `single claim after an award or claim as a joint claimant, or joint claim after an award or claim as a member of a different couple` IS `this is a single claim after a joint one, or a joint one after a different couple's`
            `portion of the original surplus or adjusted surplus apportioned to the claim by the Secretary of State` IS IF `the Secretary of State has apportioned the surplus` THEN JUST `the portion apportioned to my claim` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 55(4). Statutory sick pay, statutory maternity, paternity, adoption, shared parental, parental bereavement and neonatal care
-- pay count as employed earnings; other benefits do not.
@export Is a payment of this benefit treated as my employed earnings (reg 55(4))?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit or statutory payment is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a payment of this benefit treated as my employed earnings` IF
    `reg 55(4) — a benefit treated as employed earnings` `the benefit`

-- reg 55. Employed earnings for an assessment period: general earnings, less the amounts counted elsewhere and the amounts exempt
-- from tax, less allowed expenses (including a service user's expenses), plus the statutory payments of reg 55(4) and a repayment of
-- tax or National Insurance contributions that reg 55(4A) counts, less income tax and National Insurance contributions you paid, your
-- relievable pension contributions and payroll giving. The seat asks for one statutory payment at a time (kind and amount).
@export What are my employed earnings for an assessment period, in pounds (reg 55)?
GIVEN `my general earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your general earnings from the employment in the assessment period, in pounds (the amount ITEPA section 7(3) defines)?
      `of which treated as earnings by the benefits code` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, was treated as earnings under Chapters 2 to 11 of Part 3 of ITEPA (benefits in kind and the like)?
      `of which exempt from income tax` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, was exempt from income tax under Part 4 of ITEPA?
      `of which allowed expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, was expenses allowed to be deducted under Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA?
      `of which expenses of being a service user` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, was expenses arising from participating as a service user?
      `I am consulted by or for a body with a duty to provide health, social care or social housing services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing?
      `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors such services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services?
      `I am consulted as a user or potential user of those services, or a carer or person affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted in your capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services?
      `I am consulted by or for the Secretary of State about social security, child support or employment and training functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of the Secretary of State in relation to the Secretary of State's functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973?
      `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors those functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions?
      `I am consulted as a person affected by those functions, or the carer of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted in your capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions, or the carer of such a person?
      `I am the carer of a person who is consulted in that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the carer of a person consulted under the first or the fourth of those questions?
      `the statutory payment I received` IS A Benefit @desc Which statutory payment or benefit did you receive in the assessment period? (If none, choose any and put 0 below.)
      `how much of it I received` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of it did you receive, in pounds?
      `a tax or National Insurance repayment I received` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you receive from HMRC as a repayment of income tax or National Insurance contributions for a tax year?
      `the repayment relates to paid work I did in that tax year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the repayment relate to paid work that you did in that tax year (work done for payment or in expectation of payment, not unpaid volunteering)?
      `the repayment is counted as my self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the repayment taken into account as your self-employed earnings under regulation 57(4)?
      `I made relievable pension contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you pay in relievable pension contributions in the assessment period?
      `I paid income tax and National Insurance on it` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you pay in the assessment period by way of income tax or primary Class 1 National Insurance contributions in respect of the employment?
      `I gave to charity through payroll giving` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, was withheld in the assessment period as donations to an approved payroll giving scheme?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my employed earnings for an assessment period` IS
    `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` `my amounts`
    WHERE
        `my amounts` MEANS `Amounts received from an employment in an assessment period` WITH
            `general earnings as defined in section 7(3) of ITEPA` IS `my general earnings`
            `of which amounts treated as earnings under Chapters 2 to 11 of Part 3 of ITEPA (the benefits code)` IS `of which treated as earnings by the benefits code`
            `of which amounts exempt from income tax under Part 4 of ITEPA` IS `of which exempt from income tax`
            `of which expenses allowed to be deducted under Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA` IS `of which allowed expenses`
            `of which expenses arising from participation as a service user` IS `of which expenses of being a service user`
            `service user participation of the person` IS `my participation`
            `benefits received` IS LIST `my statutory payment`
            `repayment of income tax or national insurance contributions received from HMRC in respect of a tax year` IS `a tax or National Insurance repayment I received`
            `work done by the person in that tax year` IS `the work I did in that tax year`
            `the repayment is taken into account as self-employed earnings under regulation 57(4)` IS `the repayment is counted as my self-employed earnings`
            `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period` IS `I made relievable pension contributions`
            `amounts paid by the person in the assessment period in respect of the employment by way of income tax or primary Class 1 contributions` IS `I paid income tax and National Insurance on it`
            `sums withheld as donations to an approved scheme under Part 12 of ITEPA (payroll giving)` IS `I gave to charity through payroll giving`
        `my participation` MEANS `Person who may be participating as a service user` WITH
            `consulted by or on behalf of a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing` IS `I am consulted by or for a body with a duty to provide health, social care or social housing services`
            `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services` IS `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors such services`
            `consulted in their capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services` IS `I am consulted as a user or potential user of those services, or a carer or person affected`
            `consulted by or on behalf of the Secretary of State in relation to the Secretary of State's functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973` IS `I am consulted by or for the Secretary of State about social security, child support or employment and training functions`
            `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions` IS `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors those functions`
            `consulted in their capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions or the carer of such a person` IS `I am consulted as a person affected by those functions, or the carer of such a person`
            `the carer of a person consulted under sub-paragraph (a) or (ab)` IS `I am the carer of a person who is consulted in that way`
        `my statutory payment` MEANS `Payment of a benefit` WITH
            `benefit` IS `the statutory payment I received`
            `amount` IS `how much of it I received`
        `the work I did in that tax year` MEANS `Work done by a person` WITH
            `work is done for payment or in expectation of payment` IS `the repayment relates to paid work I did in that tax year`
            `person is engaged by a charitable or voluntary organisation, or as a volunteer` IS FALSE
            `payment received or due to be paid is only in respect of expenses` IS FALSE

-- reg 56. If you have had employed earnings and have withdrawn your labour in furtherance of a trade dispute (and your contract has
-- not been terminated), you are treated as having the employed earnings you would have had but for the dispute.
@export What employed earnings am I treated as having if I am on strike (reg 56)?
GIVEN `I have had employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you had employed earnings?
      `I have withdrawn my labour in a trade dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you withdrawn your labour in furtherance of a trade dispute?
      `my contract of service has been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your contract of service been terminated?
      `what I would have earned but for the dispute` IS A NUMBER @desc What employed earnings, in pounds, would you have had were it not for the trade dispute?
      `what I do earn` IS A NUMBER @desc What employed earnings, in pounds, do you actually have?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What employed earnings am I treated as having if I am on strike` IS
    `reg 56 — the employed earnings assumed for an employee involved in a trade dispute` `my dispute`
    WHERE
        `my dispute` MEANS `Employee involved in a trade dispute` WITH
            `the person has had employed earnings` IS `I have had employed earnings`
            `the person has withdrawn their labour in furtherance of a trade dispute` IS `I have withdrawn my labour in a trade dispute`
            `the person's contract of service has been terminated` IS `my contract of service has been terminated`
            `employed earnings the person would have had were it not for the trade dispute` IS `what I would have earned but for the dispute`
            `employed earnings the person has` IS `what I do earn`

-- reg 57(2). Self-employed earnings for an assessment period: receipts (cash, in kind, refunds, and the assets of reg 57(5)) less allowed
-- expenses, your share where it is a partnership, less what you paid HMRC, less relievable pension contributions not already deducted,
-- less unused losses. The seat asks about one business at a time and takes no asset receipts (ask the question about reg 57(5)
-- separately); the module adds several businesses together.
@export What are my self-employed earnings for an assessment period, in pounds (reg 57(2))?
GIVEN `what my business received in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did your trade, profession or vocation actually receive in the assessment period?
      `the value of what it received in kind` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value, in pounds, of any receipts in kind?
      `a tax refund relating to the business` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you receive as a refund or repayment of income tax, VAT or National Insurance contributions relating to the business? (0 if none)
      `the expenses I am allowed for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, are your allowed expenses for the assessment period (see the questions about regulations 58 and 59)?
      `the business is a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business carried on in a partnership?
      `my share of the partnership profit or loss` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what fraction of the profit or loss is yours? (for example 0.5 for a half; 0 if it is not a partnership)
      `what I paid HMRC for the business` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you pay HMRC in the assessment period by way of National Insurance contributions or income tax in respect of the business?
      `my relievable pension contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you pay in relievable pension contributions in the assessment period?
      `those contributions were already deducted from my employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were those contributions already deducted when your employed earnings were worked out?
      `my unused losses from earlier periods` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your total of unused losses, in pounds, from earlier assessment periods and from the 12 months before your claim? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my self-employed earnings for an assessment period` IS
    `reg 57(2) — the self-employed earnings for an assessment period` `my self-employed earnings`
    WHERE
        `my self-employed earnings` MEANS `Self-employed earnings considered under regulation 57` WITH
            `trades, professions or vocations carried on by the person in the assessment period` IS LIST `my business`
            `payments made by the person to HMRC in the assessment period by way of national insurance contributions or income tax in respect of any trade, profession or vocation` IS `what I paid HMRC for the business`
            `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period` IS `my relievable pension contributions`
            `a deduction has been made in respect of those contributions in calculating the person's employed earnings` IS `those contributions were already deducted from my employed earnings`
            `unused losses, oldest first` IS IF `my unused losses from earlier periods` GREATER THAN 0 THEN LIST `my unused losses from earlier periods` ELSE EMPTY
        `my business` MEANS `Trade, profession or vocation carried on in an assessment period` WITH
            `actual receipts in the assessment period` IS `what my business received in the period`
            `receipts in kind (their value)` IS `the value of what it received in kind`
            `any refund or repayment of income tax, value added tax or national insurance contributions relating to the trade, profession or vocation` IS `a tax refund relating to the business`
            `assets treated as receipts of the assessment period` IS EMPTY
            `amounts allowed as expenses under regulation 58 or 59` IS `the expenses I am allowed for the period`
            `share of the profit or loss attributable to the person, where the trade, profession or vocation is carried on in a partnership` IS IF `the business is a partnership` THEN JUST `my share of the partnership profit or loss` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 57(5). If you sold, or stopped using for the business, an asset whose purchase you deducted as an expense in an earlier
-- assessment period, you are treated as receiving the sale proceeds or, if you did not sell it, what you would receive at its current
-- market value.
@export What am I treated as receiving for a business asset I sold or stopped using, in pounds (reg 57(5))?
GIVEN `I deducted the cost of buying it as an expense in an earlier period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deduct the cost of buying the asset as an expense in an earlier assessment period?
      `I have sold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you sold the asset?
      `I have stopped using it for the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you stopped using the asset for the business?
      `what I sold it for` IS A NUMBER @desc What did you sell it for, in pounds? (0 if you have not sold it)
      `what it would fetch at market value` IS A NUMBER @desc What would you receive for it, in pounds, if you sold it at its current market value?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What am I treated as receiving for a business asset I sold or stopped using` IS
    `reg 57(5) — the amount treated as a receipt` `my asset`
    WHERE
        `my asset` MEANS `Asset the purchase of which was deducted as an expense` WITH
            `the purchase was deducted as an expense in an earlier assessment period` IS `I deducted the cost of buying it as an expense in an earlier period`
            `the asset has been sold` IS `I have sold it`
            `the asset has ceased to be used for the purposes of the trade, profession or vocation` IS `I have stopped using it for the business`
            `proceeds of sale of the asset` IS `what I sold it for`
            `amount that would be received for the asset if it were sold at its current market value` IS `what it would fetch at market value`

-- reg 57A(1)(a). If the result of reg 57(2) is a loss, the loss is carried forward as an unused loss.
@export What loss do I have for the assessment period, in pounds (reg 57A(1))?
GIVEN `what my business received in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did your trade, profession or vocation actually receive in the assessment period?
      `the value of what it received in kind` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value, in pounds, of any receipts in kind?
      `a tax refund relating to the business` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you receive as a refund or repayment of income tax, VAT or National Insurance contributions relating to the business? (0 if none)
      `the expenses I am allowed for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, are your allowed expenses for the assessment period (see the questions about regulations 58 and 59)?
      `the business is a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business carried on in a partnership?
      `my share of the partnership profit or loss` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what fraction of the profit or loss is yours? (for example 0.5 for a half; 0 if it is not a partnership)
      `what I paid HMRC for the business` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you pay HMRC in the assessment period by way of National Insurance contributions or income tax in respect of the business?
      `my relievable pension contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you pay in relievable pension contributions in the assessment period?
      `those contributions were already deducted from my employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were those contributions already deducted when your employed earnings were worked out?
      `my unused losses from earlier periods` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your total of unused losses, in pounds, from earlier assessment periods and from the 12 months before your claim? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What loss do I have for the assessment period` IS
    `reg 57A(1)(a) — the loss for the assessment period` `my self-employed earnings`
    WHERE
        `my self-employed earnings` MEANS `Self-employed earnings considered under regulation 57` WITH
            `trades, professions or vocations carried on by the person in the assessment period` IS LIST `my business`
            `payments made by the person to HMRC in the assessment period by way of national insurance contributions or income tax in respect of any trade, profession or vocation` IS `what I paid HMRC for the business`
            `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period` IS `my relievable pension contributions`
            `a deduction has been made in respect of those contributions in calculating the person's employed earnings` IS `those contributions were already deducted from my employed earnings`
            `unused losses, oldest first` IS IF `my unused losses from earlier periods` GREATER THAN 0 THEN LIST `my unused losses from earlier periods` ELSE EMPTY
        `my business` MEANS `Trade, profession or vocation carried on in an assessment period` WITH
            `actual receipts in the assessment period` IS `what my business received in the period`
            `receipts in kind (their value)` IS `the value of what it received in kind`
            `any refund or repayment of income tax, value added tax or national insurance contributions relating to the trade, profession or vocation` IS `a tax refund relating to the business`
            `assets treated as receipts of the assessment period` IS EMPTY
            `amounts allowed as expenses under regulation 58 or 59` IS `the expenses I am allowed for the period`
            `share of the profit or loss attributable to the person, where the trade, profession or vocation is carried on in a partnership` IS IF `the business is a partnership` THEN JUST `my share of the partnership profit or loss` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 57A(3). Assessment periods under a previous award count as assessment periods under the current award if the previous award
-- ended within 6 months before the new one, you provide the information required, and the Secretary of State so treats them.
@export Do my earlier assessment periods count under my new award (reg 57A(3))?
GIVEN `the last day my previous award applied` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which you were entitled under your previous award?
      `the first day my new award applies` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day on which you are entitled under your new award?
      `I provide the information required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide the information that the Secretary of State requires?
      `the Secretary of State treats them as assessment periods under the new award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State treated those assessment periods and months as assessment periods under your current award?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my earlier assessment periods count under my new award` IF
    `reg 57A(3) — the previous assessment periods count as assessment periods under the current award` `the last day my previous award applied` `the first day my new award applies` `I provide the information required` `the Secretary of State treats them as assessment periods under the new award`

-- reg 58. How much of a payment you made for your business you may deduct: an ordinary payment, the part wholly and exclusively
-- incurred for the business (or the identifiable proportion where there were several purposes), nothing if unreasonable; interest on a
-- loan, up to 41 pounds in a payment; nothing for capital repayments, entertainment, a car, or buying a non-depreciating asset; a
-- motor vehicle that is not a car, or your home, only if you do not take the flat-rate deduction under reg 59.
@export How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct, in pounds (reg 58)?
GIVEN `what the payment was for` IS A `Kind of payment for a trade, profession or vocation` @desc What was the payment for?
      `the amount I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you pay in the assessment period (including any VAT)?
      `it was wholly and exclusively for the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it incurred wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the business?
      `it was for more than one purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it incurred for more than one purpose?
      `the proportion for the business is identifiable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, can you identify the proportion that was wholly and exclusively for the business?
      `the proportion that was for the business` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of it was for the business? (for example 0.25; 0 if you cannot identify it)
      `it was incurred unreasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it incurred unreasonably?
      `I take the flat-rate deduction in regulation 59 instead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking the flat-rate deduction under regulation 59 instead of the actual expense?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct` IS
    `reg 58 — the deduction allowed for a payment` `my payment`
    WHERE
        `my payment` MEANS `Payment made in the assessment period for a trade, profession or vocation` WITH
            `kind of payment` IS `what the payment was for`
            `amount paid in the assessment period (which may include value added tax)` IS `the amount I paid`
            `wholly and exclusively incurred for the purposes of the trade, profession or vocation` IS `it was wholly and exclusively for the business`
            `incurred for more than one purpose` IS `it was for more than one purpose`
            `identifiable proportion that has been wholly and exclusively incurred for the purposes of the trade, profession or vocation` IS IF `the proportion for the business is identifiable` THEN JUST `the proportion that was for the business` ELSE NOTHING
            `incurred unreasonably` IS `it was incurred unreasonably`
            `the person takes the deduction under regulation 59 instead of the actual expense` IS `I take the flat-rate deduction in regulation 59 instead`

-- reg 59(2). Flat-rate deduction for using a vehicle: 45p a mile for the first 833 miles in a car, van or other motor vehicle other than a motorcycle in the
-- assessment period and 25p after that, and 24p a mile on a motorcycle.
@export What deduction can I take for the miles I travelled for my business, in pounds (reg 59(2))?
GIVEN `miles I drove in a car, van or other motor vehicle for the business` IS A NUMBER @desc How many miles did you cover for the business in the assessment period in a car, van or other motor vehicle (apart from a motorcycle)?
      `miles I rode a motorcycle for the business` IS A NUMBER @desc How many miles did you cover for the business in the assessment period on a motorcycle?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What deduction can I take for the miles I travelled for my business` IS
    `reg 59(2) — the deduction for mileage` `miles I drove in a car, van or other motor vehicle for the business` `miles I rode a motorcycle for the business`

-- reg 59(3). Flat-rate deduction for using your home: 10 pounds for at least 25 and up to 50 hours of income generating activity in the
-- assessment period, 18 pounds for more than 50 and up to 100, 26 pounds for more than 100; nothing below 25 hours.
@export What deduction can I take for working from my home, in pounds (reg 59(3))?
GIVEN `hours I worked from home on the business` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you spend in the assessment period on income generating activities for the business?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What deduction can I take for working from my home` IS
    `reg 59(3) — the deduction for use of the person's home` `hours I worked from home on the business`

-- reg 59(4). Where your business premises are also your home, the deduction is reduced by 350 pounds for one other person living there,
-- 500 for two and 650 for three or more.
@export By how much is my deduction reduced because others live in my business premises, in pounds (reg 59(4))?
GIVEN `the number of people who live in the premises` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people occupy the premises for their personal use?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much is my deduction reduced because others live in my business premises` IS
    `reg 59(4) — the reduction for personal use of the premises` `the number of people who live in the premises`

-- reg 60(1), (2). If you, or your employer on your behalf, deprived you of earned income, you are treated as having it if it was to
-- get universal credit or more of it; the purpose is treated as existing where universal credit in fact followed and the Secretary of
-- State thinks that was a foreseeable and intended consequence.
@export Am I treated as having earned income that I was deprived of (reg 60(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the amount of earned income I was deprived of` IS A NUMBER @desc How much earned income, in pounds, were you deprived of?
      `I deprived myself of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deprive yourself of it?
      `my employer arranged for me to be deprived of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer arrange for you to be deprived of it?
      `it was to get universal credit or more of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done in order to secure universal credit, or a higher amount of it?
      `universal credit or more of it did in fact result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did entitlement, or higher entitlement, to universal credit in fact result?
      `the Secretary of State thinks that was foreseeable and intended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the opinion of the Secretary of State, was that a foreseeable and intended consequence?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Am I treated as having earned income that I was deprived of` IS
    `reg 60(1) — the earned income the person is treated as possessing` `my deprivation`
    WHERE
        `my deprivation` MEANS `Deprivation of earned income` WITH
            `amount of the earned income of which the person has been deprived` IS `the amount of earned income I was deprived of`
            `the person has deprived themselves of earned income` IS `I deprived myself of it`
            `the person's employer has arranged for the person to be deprived of earned income` IS `my employer arranged for me to be deprived of it`
            `the deprivation was for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit` IS `it was to get universal credit or more of it`
            `entitlement or higher entitlement to universal credit did in fact result` IS `universal credit or more of it did in fact result`
            `in the opinion of the Secretary of State this was a foreseeable and intended consequence of the deprivation` IS `the Secretary of State thinks that was foreseeable and intended`

-- reg 60(3), (4). If you provide services to someone who pays nothing, or less than is paid for comparable services, and could have
-- paid more, you are treated as having received reasonable remuneration for them; but not where you are engaged by a charity or
-- voluntary organisation and it is reasonable for the services to be free or cheap, or you are a service user, or on an approved
-- employment or training programme.
@export What payment am I treated as having received for services I provide (reg 60(3), (4))?
GIVEN `what the other person pays me for the services` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, does the other person pay you for the services?
      `what comparable services are paid in my area` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, would be paid for comparable services in the same location?
      `the other person could afford to pay for or pay more for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the other person's means sufficient to pay for, or pay more for, the services?
      `what would be reasonable pay for them` IS A NUMBER @desc What remuneration, in pounds, would be reasonable for the services?
      `I am engaged by a charity or voluntary organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you engaged to provide the services by a charitable or voluntary organisation?
      `the Secretary of State thinks it is reasonable for them to be free or cheap` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that it is reasonable for the services to be free of charge or at less than the rate for comparable services?
      `the services are part of an approved employment or training programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the services provided under or in connection with your participation in an employment or training programme approved by the Secretary of State?
      `I am consulted by or for a body with a duty to provide health, social care or social housing services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing?
      `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors such services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services?
      `I am consulted as a user or potential user of those services, or a carer or person affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted in your capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services?
      `I am consulted by or for the Secretary of State about social security, child support or employment and training functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of the Secretary of State in relation to the Secretary of State's functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973?
      `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors those functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions?
      `I am consulted as a person affected by those functions, or the carer of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you consulted in your capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions, or the carer of such a person?
      `I am the carer of a person who is consulted in that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the carer of a person consulted under the first or the fourth of those questions?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What payment am I treated as having received for services I provide` IS
    `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` `the services I provide` `the exceptions that may apply`
    WHERE
        `the services I provide` MEANS `Services provided by a person for another person` WITH
            `payment the other person makes for those services` IS `what the other person pays me for the services`
            `amount that would be paid for comparable services in the same location` IS `what comparable services are paid in my area`
            `the means of the other person were sufficient to pay for, or pay more for, those services` IS `the other person could afford to pay for or pay more for them`
            `remuneration that would be reasonable for the provision of those services` IS `what would be reasonable pay for them`
        `the exceptions that may apply` MEANS `Services to which regulation 60(3) may not apply` WITH
            `the person is engaged to provide the services by a charitable or voluntary organisation` IS `I am engaged by a charity or voluntary organisation`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is reasonable to provide the services free of charge or at less than the rate that would be paid for comparable services in the same location` IS `the Secretary of State thinks it is reasonable for them to be free or cheap`
            `service user participation of the person` IS `my participation`
            `the services are provided under or in connection with a person's participation in an employment or training programme approved by the Secretary of State` IS `the services are part of an approved employment or training programme`
        `my participation` MEANS `Person who may be participating as a service user` WITH
            `consulted by or on behalf of a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing` IS `I am consulted by or for a body with a duty to provide health, social care or social housing services`
            `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services` IS `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors such services`
            `consulted in their capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services` IS `I am consulted as a user or potential user of those services, or a carer or person affected`
            `consulted by or on behalf of the Secretary of State in relation to the Secretary of State's functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973` IS `I am consulted by or for the Secretary of State about social security, child support or employment and training functions`
            `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions` IS `I am consulted by or for a body that researches or monitors those functions`
            `consulted in their capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions or the carer of such a person` IS `I am consulted as a person affected by those functions, or the carer of such a person`
            `the carer of a person consulted under sub-paragraph (a) or (ab)` IS `I am the carer of a person who is consulted in that way`

GIVEN period IS A MAYBE `Start-up period`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`seat uc2 — the last day of a start-up period, if there is one` period MEANS
    CONSIDER period
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST startup THEN JUST (startup's `last day of the start-up period`)

-- reg 61(1). You must provide the information needed to calculate your earned income when the Secretary of State requires it,
-- unless it is earned income from an employment whose employer is a Real Time Information employer.
@export Must I give the Secretary of State information to work out my earned income (reg 61(1))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State asks me for the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State require the information from you at this time?
      `the income is from a job with a Real Time Information employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the earned income from an employment whose employer is a Real Time Information employer (one who reports your pay to HMRC each time they pay you)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Secretary of State information to work out my earned income` IF
    `reg 61(1) — the person must provide the information for calculating their earned income` `the Secretary of State asks me for the information` `the income is from a job with a Real Time Information employer`

-- reg 61(2), (3). The employed earnings from a job are based on what the employer reports to HMRC (Real Time Information), unless
-- the Secretary of State thinks the employer is unlikely to report accurately or in time, a reported payment looks incorrect, or
-- nothing was received from HMRC and that is likely a failure to report.
@export Are my employed earnings from this job based on what my employer reports to HMRC (reg 61(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my employer is a Real Time Information employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer a Real Time Information employer?
      `the Secretary of State thinks my employer is unlikely to report accurately or in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that your employer is unlikely to report information to HMRC in a sufficiently accurate or timely manner?
      `a payment reported to HMRC looks incorrect to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that the amount of a payment reported to HMRC is incorrect, or fails to reflect the definition of employed earnings in a material respect?
      `no information came from HMRC and the Secretary of State thinks that is a failure to report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no information received from HMRC in the assessment period, and does the Secretary of State consider that is likely to be because of a failure to report?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my employed earnings from this job based on what my employer reports to HMRC` IF
    `reg 61(2) — the employed earnings are based on Real Time Information` `my job`
    WHERE
        `my job` MEANS `Employment considered under regulation 61` WITH
            `the employer is a Real Time Information employer` IS `my employer is a Real Time Information employer`
            `the Secretary of State considers that the employer is unlikely to report information to HMRC in a sufficiently accurate or timely manner` IS `the Secretary of State thinks my employer is unlikely to report accurately or in time`
            `it appears to the Secretary of State that the amount of a payment reported to HMRC is incorrect, or fails to reflect the definition of employed earnings in regulation 55 in some material respect` IS `a payment reported to HMRC looks incorrect to the Secretary of State`
            `no information is received from HMRC in the assessment period and the Secretary of State considers that this is likely to be because of a failure to report information` IS `no information came from HMRC and the Secretary of State thinks that is a failure to report`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `amount of employed earnings from the employment based on the information reported to HMRC and received by the Secretary of State from HMRC in the assessment period` IS NOTHING
            `amount of employed earnings from the employment determined in accordance with regulation 55` IS 0

-- reg 61(2), (4). The employed earnings from a job for an assessment period: the amount reported to HMRC and received from HMRC
-- (nil if none was received) where Real Time Information applies; otherwise the amount worked out under regulation 55.
@export What are my employed earnings from this job for the assessment period, in pounds (reg 61(2), (4))?
GIVEN `my employer is a Real Time Information employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer a Real Time Information employer?
      `the Secretary of State thinks my employer is unlikely to report accurately or in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that your employer is unlikely to report information to HMRC in a sufficiently accurate or timely manner?
      `a payment reported to HMRC looks incorrect to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that the amount of a payment reported to HMRC is incorrect, or fails to reflect the definition of employed earnings in a material respect?
      `no information came from HMRC and the Secretary of State thinks that is a failure to report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no information received from HMRC in the assessment period, and does the Secretary of State consider that is likely to be because of a failure to report?
      `HMRC has told the Secretary of State what my employer reported` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State received from HMRC, in the assessment period, the information your employer reported?
      `the amount my employer reported to HMRC` IS A NUMBER @desc What employed earnings, in pounds, does that information show? (0 if none was received)
      `my employed earnings worked out under regulation 55` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your employed earnings, in pounds, worked out under regulation 55 (see the question about it above)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my employed earnings from this job for the assessment period` IS
    `reg 61(2) and (4) — the employed earnings from the employment for an assessment period` `my job`
    WHERE
        `my job` MEANS `Employment considered under regulation 61` WITH
            `the employer is a Real Time Information employer` IS `my employer is a Real Time Information employer`
            `the Secretary of State considers that the employer is unlikely to report information to HMRC in a sufficiently accurate or timely manner` IS `the Secretary of State thinks my employer is unlikely to report accurately or in time`
            `it appears to the Secretary of State that the amount of a payment reported to HMRC is incorrect, or fails to reflect the definition of employed earnings in regulation 55 in some material respect` IS `a payment reported to HMRC looks incorrect to the Secretary of State`
            `no information is received from HMRC in the assessment period and the Secretary of State considers that this is likely to be because of a failure to report information` IS `no information came from HMRC and the Secretary of State thinks that is a failure to report`
            `amount of employed earnings from the employment based on the information reported to HMRC and received by the Secretary of State from HMRC in the assessment period` IS IF `HMRC has told the Secretary of State what my employer reported` THEN JUST `the amount my employer reported to HMRC` ELSE NOTHING
            `amount of employed earnings from the employment determined in accordance with regulation 55` IS `my employed earnings worked out under regulation 55`

-- reg 61(5). A payment reported late, or in the wrong assessment period, counts in the assessment period in which it was received if
-- the Secretary of State so determines; otherwise in the period in which it was reported. The answer is the first day of that period.
@export In which assessment period is my late or misplaced payment counted: on what date does that period begin (reg 61(5))?
GIVEN `the payment was reported late or in the wrong period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment reported late, or in the wrong assessment period?
      `the Secretary of State has decided it counts in the period I received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State determined that the payment is to be treated as employed earnings in the assessment period in which you received it?
      `first day of the period it was reported in` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the assessment period in which it was reported begin?
      `last day of the period it was reported in` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the assessment period in which it was reported end?
      `first day of the period I received it in` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the assessment period in which you received it begin?
      `last day of the period I received it in` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the assessment period in which you received it end?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which assessment period is my late or misplaced payment counted` IS
    (`reg 61(5) — the assessment period in which the payment is treated as employed earnings` `my late payment`)'s `first day`
    WHERE
        `my late payment` MEANS `Payment of employed earnings that may have been reported late` WITH
            `the payment has been reported late, or otherwise reported in the wrong assessment period` IS `the payment was reported late or in the wrong period`
            `the Secretary of State determines that the payment is to be treated as employed earnings in the assessment period in which it was received` IS `the Secretary of State has decided it counts in the period I received it`
            `assessment period in which the payment was reported` IS `the period it was reported in`
            `assessment period in which the payment was received` IS `the period I received it in`
        `the period it was reported in` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `first day of the period it was reported in`
            `last day` IS `last day of the period it was reported in`
        `the period I received it in` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `first day of the period I received it in`
            `last day` IS `last day of the period I received it in`

-- reg 61(6). Where you are paid regularly each month and more than one payment is reported in one assessment period, the Secretary of
-- State may decide that one of them counts in a different assessment period to keep a regular pattern. The answer is the first day of
-- the period in which it counts.
@export In which assessment period is one of two payments reported together counted: on what date does that period begin (reg 61(6))?
GIVEN `I am paid regularly each month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid on a regular monthly basis in the employment?
      `two payments were reported in one period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is more than one payment in relation to that employment reported in the same assessment period?
      `the Secretary of State has moved one of them to another period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State determined, to maintain a regular pattern, that one of those payments is to be treated as employed earnings in respect of a different assessment period?
      `first day of the period they were reported in` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the assessment period in which they were reported begin?
      `last day of the period they were reported in` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the assessment period in which they were reported end?
      `first day of the other period` IS A DATE @desc If one has been moved, on what date does the other assessment period begin?
      `last day of the other period` IS A DATE @desc If one has been moved, on what date does the other assessment period end?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which assessment period is one of two payments reported together counted` IS
    (`reg 61(6) — the assessment period in which one of the payments is treated as employed earnings` `my monthly payments`)'s `first day`
    WHERE
        `my monthly payments` MEANS `Regular monthly payment that may be moved to a different assessment period` WITH
            `the person is engaged in an employment where they are paid on a regular monthly basis` IS `I am paid regularly each month`
            `more than one payment in relation to that employment is reported in the same assessment period` IS `two payments were reported in one period`
            `the Secretary of State determines, for the purposes of maintaining a regular pattern, that one of those payments is to be treated as employed earnings in respect of a different assessment period` IS `the Secretary of State has moved one of them to another period`
            `assessment period in which the payment was reported` IS `the period they were reported in`
            `the different assessment period` IS IF `the Secretary of State has moved one of them to another period` THEN JUST `the other period` ELSE NOTHING
        `the period they were reported in` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `first day of the period they were reported in`
            `last day` IS `last day of the period they were reported in`
        `the other period` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `first day of the other period`
            `last day` IS `last day of the other period`

-- reg 61(7). Where the Secretary of State has made a determination under reg 61(4), (5) or (6), the employed earnings are adjusted as
-- necessary to avoid duplication or to keep a regular pattern.
@export What are my employed earnings after the Secretary of State adjusts them, in pounds (reg 61(7))?
GIVEN `my employed earnings before any adjustment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your employed earnings, in pounds, before any adjustment?
      `the Secretary of State has made a determination under regulation 61(4), (5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State made a determination under paragraph (4), (5) or (6) of regulation 61?
      `the adjustment the Secretary of State makes` IS A NUMBER @desc What adjustment, in pounds, does the Secretary of State make (positive or negative)? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my employed earnings after the Secretary of State adjusts them` IS
    `reg 61(7) — the employed earnings after any consequential adjustment` `my employed earnings before any adjustment` `the Secretary of State has made a determination under regulation 61(4), (5) or (6)` `the adjustment the Secretary of State makes`

-- reg 62. The minimum income floor: if you are in gainful self-employment and in the work-related group "subject to all work-related
-- requirements", you are treated as having at least the individual threshold (or, for a couple, an amount that brings your joint income to
-- the couple threshold), each less the tax and National Insurance the Secretary of State thinks appropriate, unless the assessment period
-- falls in your start-up period. The surplus earnings of reg 54A are added to your earned income, or your partner's, whichever is
-- better for you.
@export How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor, in pounds (reg 62)?
GIVEN `I am in gainful self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in gainful self-employment (see the question about regulation 64)?
      `my work-related group` IS A `Work-related group` @desc Which work-related group would you fall within, apart from the minimum income floor?
      `the basis of my claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Do you claim alone, jointly with your partner, or alone while being a member of a couple?
      `my earned income for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income, in pounds, for the assessment period?
      `my partner's earned income for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your partner's earned income, in pounds, for the assessment period? (0 if you have no partner)
      `the individual threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the individual threshold, in pounds, set by regulation 90(2)?
      `the couple threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the couple threshold, in pounds, set by regulation 90(3)?
      `tax and National Insurance deducted from the individual threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, does the Secretary of State consider appropriate for income tax and National Insurance contributions to deduct from the individual threshold?
      `tax and National Insurance deducted from the couple threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, does the Secretary of State consider appropriate for income tax and National Insurance contributions to deduct from the couple threshold?
      `surplus earnings counted as my earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much surplus earnings, in pounds, are treated as your earned income under regulation 54A? (0 if none)
      `first day of the assessment period` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the assessment period begin?
      `last day of the assessment period` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the assessment period end?
      `I have a start-up period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a start-up period (see the question about regulation 63)?
      `first day of my start-up period` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date does it begin?
      `last day of my start-up period` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date does it end?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` IS
    `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` `my self-employment`
    WHERE
        `my self-employment` MEANS `Claimant considered under regulation 62` WITH
            `claimant in gainful self-employment` IS `I am in gainful self-employment`
            `work-related group the claimant would fall within, apart from regulation 62 or regulation 90` IS `my work-related group`
            `basis of the claim` IS `the basis of my claim`
            `earned income of the claimant for the assessment period` IS `my earned income for the period`
            `earned income of the claimant's partner for the assessment period` IS `my partner's earned income for the period`
            `individual threshold (regulation 90(2))` IS `the individual threshold`
            `couple threshold (regulation 90(3))` IS `the couple threshold`
            `amount for income tax and national insurance contributions that the Secretary of State considers appropriate to deduct from the individual threshold` IS `tax and National Insurance deducted from the individual threshold`
            `amount for income tax and national insurance contributions that the Secretary of State considers appropriate to deduct from the couple threshold` IS `tax and National Insurance deducted from the couple threshold`
            `surplus earnings treated as earned income under regulation 54A` IS `surplus earnings counted as my earned income`
            `assessment period` IS `this assessment period`
            `start-up period` IS IF `I have a start-up period` THEN JUST `my start-up period` ELSE NOTHING
        `this assessment period` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `first day of the assessment period`
            `last day` IS `last day of the assessment period`
        `my start-up period` MEANS `Start-up period` WITH
            `first day of the start-up period` IS `first day of my start-up period`
            `last day of the start-up period` IS `last day of my start-up period`

-- reg 62(1). The minimum income floor applies to you if you are in gainful self-employment and your work-related group would be
-- "subject to all work-related requirements".
@export Does the minimum income floor apply to me (reg 62(1))?
GIVEN `I am in gainful self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in gainful self-employment (see the question about regulation 64)?
      `my work-related group` IS A `Work-related group` @desc Which work-related group would you fall within, apart from the minimum income floor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the minimum income floor apply to me` IF
    `reg 62(1) — this regulation applies to the claimant` `my self-employment`
    WHERE
        `my self-employment` MEANS `Claimant considered under regulation 62` WITH
            `claimant in gainful self-employment` IS `I am in gainful self-employment`
            `work-related group the claimant would fall within, apart from regulation 62 or regulation 90` IS `my work-related group`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `basis of the claim` IS `a single claimant`
            `earned income of the claimant for the assessment period` IS 0
            `earned income of the claimant's partner for the assessment period` IS 0
            `individual threshold (regulation 90(2))` IS 0
            `couple threshold (regulation 90(3))` IS 0
            `amount for income tax and national insurance contributions that the Secretary of State considers appropriate to deduct from the individual threshold` IS 0
            `amount for income tax and national insurance contributions that the Secretary of State considers appropriate to deduct from the couple threshold` IS 0
            `surplus earnings treated as earned income under regulation 54A` IS 0
            `assessment period` IS `this assessment period`
            `start-up period` IS NOTHING
        `this assessment period` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `first day` IS YMD 1900 1 1
            `last day` IS YMD 1900 1 1

-- reg 62(5). The minimum income floor does not apply in an assessment period that falls, in whole or in part, in the start-up period.
@export Does my assessment period fall in my start-up period, so that the minimum income floor is not applied (reg 62(5))?
GIVEN `first day of the assessment period` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the assessment period begin?
      `last day of the assessment period` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the assessment period end?
      `I have a start-up period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a start-up period (see the question about regulation 63)?
      `first day of my start-up period` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date does it begin?
      `last day of my start-up period` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date does it end?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my assessment period fall in my start-up period` IF
    `reg 62(5) — the assessment period is within or touches a start-up period` `my self-employment`
    WHERE
        `my self-employment` MEANS `Claimant considered under regulation 62` WITH
            `assessment period` IS `this assessment period`
            `start-up period` IS IF `I have a start-up period` THEN JUST `my start-up period` ELSE NOTHING
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `claimant in gainful self-employment` IS FALSE
            `work-related group the claimant would fall within, apart from regulation 62 or regulation 90` IS `subject to no work-related requirements`
            `basis of the claim` IS `a single claimant`
            `earned income of the claimant for the assessment period` IS 0
            `earned income of the claimant's partner for the assessment period` IS 0
            `individual threshold (regulation 90(2))` IS 0
            `couple threshold (regulation 90(3))` IS 0
            `amount for income tax and national insurance contributions that the Secretary of State considers appropriate to deduct from the individual threshold` IS 0
            `amount for income tax and national insurance contributions that the Secretary of State considers appropriate to deduct from the couple threshold` IS 0
            `surplus earnings treated as earned income under regulation 54A` IS 0
        `this assessment period` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `first day of the assessment period`
            `last day` IS `last day of the assessment period`
        `my start-up period` MEANS `Start-up period` WITH
            `first day of the start-up period` IS `first day of my start-up period`
            `last day of the start-up period` IS `last day of my start-up period`

-- reg 63(1), (2). A start-up period applies if regulation 62 has not previously applied to you for this business and you are taking active
-- steps to raise your earnings to your threshold; an earlier start-up period bars a new one unless it began more than 5 years before and was for a
-- different business you have stopped.
@export Do I have a start-up period (reg 63)?
GIVEN `first day of the period in which I was found in gainful self-employment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the assessment period begin in which the Secretary of State determined that you are in gainful self-employment?
      `last day of the period in which I was found in gainful self-employment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that assessment period end?
      `the minimum income floor has applied to me before for this business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has regulation 62 previously applied to you in relation to the trade, profession or vocation which is now your main employment?
      `I am taking active steps to raise my earnings to my threshold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking active steps to increase your earnings from that employment to the level of your individual threshold?
      `I have had a start-up period before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a start-up period previously applied to you?
      `the day that earlier start-up period began` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did it begin? (any date if none)
      `that earlier start-up period was for a different business I have stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that earlier start-up period apply to a different trade, profession or vocation which you have ceased to carry on?
      `the Secretary of State has ended my start-up period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State terminated your start-up period?
      `the day the Secretary of State ended it` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (any date if not)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a start-up period` IF
    `reg 63(1) — a start-up period applies` `my start-up period`
    WHERE
        `my start-up period` MEANS `Start-up period considered under regulation 63` WITH
            `assessment period in which the Secretary of State determines that the claimant is in gainful self-employment` IS `the period I was found in gainful self-employment`
            `regulation 62 has previously applied to the claimant in relation to the trade, profession or vocation which is currently the claimant's main employment` IS `the minimum income floor has applied to me before for this business`
            `the claimant is taking active steps to increase their earnings from that employment to the level of the claimant's individual threshold` IS `I am taking active steps to raise my earnings to my threshold`
            `a start-up period has previously applied in relation to the claimant` IS `I have had a start-up period before`
            `date on which that previous start-up period began` IS IF `I have had a start-up period before` THEN JUST `the day that earlier start-up period began` ELSE NOTHING
            `that previous start-up period applied in relation to a different trade, profession or vocation which the claimant has ceased to carry on` IS `that earlier start-up period was for a different business I have stopped`
            `date on which the Secretary of State terminated the start-up period` IS IF `the Secretary of State has ended my start-up period` THEN JUST `the day the Secretary of State ended it` ELSE NOTHING
        `the period I was found in gainful self-employment` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `first day of the period in which I was found in gainful self-employment`
            `last day` IS `last day of the period in which I was found in gainful self-employment`

-- reg 63. A start-up period lasts 12 months from the first day of the assessment period in which you are found in gainful self-employment,
-- or until the Secretary of State terminates it if that is earlier. The answer is the last day.
@export On what date does my start-up period end (reg 63)?
GIVEN `first day of the period in which I was found in gainful self-employment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the assessment period begin in which the Secretary of State determined that you are in gainful self-employment?
      `last day of the period in which I was found in gainful self-employment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that assessment period end?
      `the minimum income floor has applied to me before for this business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has regulation 62 previously applied to you in relation to the trade, profession or vocation which is now your main employment?
      `I am taking active steps to raise my earnings to my threshold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking active steps to increase your earnings from that employment to the level of your individual threshold?
      `I have had a start-up period before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a start-up period previously applied to you?
      `the day that earlier start-up period began` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did it begin? (any date if none)
      `that earlier start-up period was for a different business I have stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that earlier start-up period apply to a different trade, profession or vocation which you have ceased to carry on?
      `the Secretary of State has ended my start-up period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State terminated your start-up period?
      `the day the Secretary of State ended it` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (any date if not)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my start-up period end` IS
    `seat uc2 — the last day of a start-up period, if there is one` (`reg 63 — the start-up period` `my start-up period`)
    WHERE
        `my start-up period` MEANS `Start-up period considered under regulation 63` WITH
            `assessment period in which the Secretary of State determines that the claimant is in gainful self-employment` IS `the period I was found in gainful self-employment`
            `regulation 62 has previously applied to the claimant in relation to the trade, profession or vocation which is currently the claimant's main employment` IS `the minimum income floor has applied to me before for this business`
            `the claimant is taking active steps to increase their earnings from that employment to the level of the claimant's individual threshold` IS `I am taking active steps to raise my earnings to my threshold`
            `a start-up period has previously applied in relation to the claimant` IS `I have had a start-up period before`
            `date on which that previous start-up period began` IS IF `I have had a start-up period before` THEN JUST `the day that earlier start-up period began` ELSE NOTHING
            `that previous start-up period applied in relation to a different trade, profession or vocation which the claimant has ceased to carry on` IS `that earlier start-up period was for a different business I have stopped`
            `date on which the Secretary of State terminated the start-up period` IS IF `the Secretary of State has ended my start-up period` THEN JUST `the day the Secretary of State ended it` ELSE NOTHING
        `the period I was found in gainful self-employment` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `first day of the period in which I was found in gainful self-employment`
            `last day` IS `last day of the period in which I was found in gainful self-employment`

-- reg 64. You are in gainful self-employment if the Secretary of State has determined that you are carrying on a trade, profession or vocation
-- as your main employment, your earnings from it are self-employed earnings, and it is organised, developed, regular and carried on in expectation of profit.
@export Am I in gainful self-employment (reg 64)?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has determined that these things are so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State determined the three matters below?
      `my business is my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you carrying on a trade, profession or vocation as your main employment?
      `my earnings from it are self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your earnings from it self-employed earnings?
      `it is organised, developed, regular and carried on in expectation of profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it organised, developed, regular and carried on in expectation of profit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in gainful self-employment` IF
    `reg 64 — the claimant is in gainful self-employment` `my business`
    WHERE
        `my business` MEANS `Claimant who may be in gainful self-employment` WITH
            `the Secretary of State has determined the matters in sub-paragraphs (a) to (c)` IS `the Secretary of State has determined that these things are so`
            `the claimant is carrying on a trade, profession or vocation as their main employment` IS `my business is my main employment`
            `their earnings from that trade, profession or vocation are self-employed earnings` IS `my earnings from it are self-employed earnings`
            `the trade, profession or vocation is organised, developed, regular and carried on in expectation of profit` IS `it is organised, developed, regular and carried on in expectation of profit`


§§ `Part 6, Chapter 3 -- Unearned income (regulations 66 to 74)`

-- reg 66(1). Unearned income is: retirement pension income; the listed benefits (jobseeker's allowance, employment and support allowance,
-- carer's allowance, carer support payment, widows' benefits, maternity allowance, industrial injuries benefit); analogous foreign
-- payments; maintenance from a spouse or former spouse; a foreign state retirement pension; student income; certain training and
-- Sports Council payments; income-protection insurance; annuity and trust income not left out by regulations 75 and 76; the income your
-- capital is treated as yielding; capital treated as income; PPF payments; and, if none of those, taxable miscellaneous income.
@export Is the income I receive unearned income (reg 66(1))?
GIVEN `it is retirement pension income that I am entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it retirement pension income to which you are entitled?
      `I am entitled to a benefit and this is it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a benefit to which you are entitled?
      `the benefit` IS A Benefit @desc If so, which benefit is it? (any, if the answer above is no)
      `it is paid under the law of another country and is like a listed benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a benefit, allowance or other payment paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom, analogous to a benefit such as jobseeker's allowance, employment and support allowance, carer's allowance or industrial injuries benefit?
      `it is maintenance paid to me under a court order or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment towards your maintenance by a spouse, civil partner, former spouse or former civil partner under a court order or an agreement for maintenance?
      `it is a state retirement pension paid by another country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a foreign state retirement pension?
      `it is student income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it student income?
      `it is a payment under the Employment and Training Act 1973 or the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973 or section 2 of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990?
      `the payment replaces universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment a substitute for universal credit?
      `the payment is for a person's living expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment for a person's living expenses?
      `it is a payment from a Sports Council out of National Lottery money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment by a Sports Council named in section 23(2) of the National Lottery etc. Act 1993, out of sums allocated to it for distribution?
      `it is paid under an insurance policy against losing income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment under an insurance policy insuring against the risk of losing income due to illness, accident or redundancy?
      `it is income from an annuity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it income from an annuity?
      `the annuity income is retirement pension income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is it retirement pension income?
      `it is income from a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it income from a trust?
      `regulation 75 leaves the annuity or trust income out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is income from an annuity or a trust disregarded under regulation 75 (compensation for personal injury; see the questions below)?
      `regulation 76 leaves the trust income out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is income from a trust disregarded under regulation 76 (special compensation schemes; see the questions below)?
      `it is income that capital is treated as yielding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it income treated as the yield from your capital by regulation 72?
      `it is capital treated as income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it capital treated as income by regulation 46(3) or (4)?
      `it is a Pension Protection Fund periodic payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a Pension Protection Fund periodic payment?
      `it is taxable miscellaneous income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it income taxable under Part 5 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 (miscellaneous income)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the income I receive unearned income` IF
    `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` `my income`
    WHERE
        `my income` MEANS `Item of income considered under regulation 66` WITH
            `retirement pension income to which the person is entitled` IS `it is retirement pension income that I am entitled to`
            `benefit to which the person is entitled` IS IF `I am entitled to a benefit and this is it` THEN JUST `the benefit` ELSE NOTHING
            `benefit, allowance or other payment paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom and analogous to a benefit mentioned in sub-paragraph (b)` IS `it is paid under the law of another country and is like a listed benefit`
            `payment towards the maintenance of the person by a spouse, civil partner, former spouse or former civil partner under a court order or an agreement for maintenance` IS `it is maintenance paid to me under a court order or agreement`
            `foreign state retirement pension` IS `it is a state retirement pension paid by another country`
            `student income` IS `it is student income`
            `payment under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973 or section 2 of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990` IS `it is a payment under the Employment and Training Act 1973 or the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990`
            `payment is a substitute for universal credit` IS `the payment replaces universal credit`
            `payment is for a person's living expenses` IS `the payment is for a person's living expenses`
            `payment by a Sports Council named in section 23(2) of the National Lottery etc. Act 1993 out of sums allocated to it for distribution` IS `it is a payment from a Sports Council out of National Lottery money`
            `payment received under an insurance policy to insure against the risk of losing income due to illness, accident or redundancy` IS `it is paid under an insurance policy against losing income`
            `income from an annuity` IS `it is income from an annuity`
            `income from an annuity is retirement pension income` IS `the annuity income is retirement pension income`
            `income from a trust` IS `it is income from a trust`
            `income from an annuity or a trust is disregarded under regulation 75` IS `regulation 75 leaves the annuity or trust income out`
            `income from a trust is disregarded under regulation 76` IS `regulation 76 leaves the trust income out`
            `income treated as the yield from the person's capital by virtue of regulation 72` IS `it is income that capital is treated as yielding`
            `capital treated as income by virtue of regulation 46(3) or (4)` IS `it is capital treated as income`
            `PPF periodic payments` IS `it is a Pension Protection Fund periodic payment`
            `income taxable under Part 5 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 (miscellaneous income)` IS `it is taxable miscellaneous income`

-- reg 66(1)(b). The listed benefits are jobseeker's allowance, employment and support allowance, carer's allowance, carer support payment,
-- widowed mother's and widowed parent's allowance, widow's pension, maternity allowance and industrial injuries benefit.
@export Is this benefit one of the listed benefits that count as unearned income (reg 66(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit or payment is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this benefit one of the listed benefits that count as unearned income` IF
    `reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `the benefit`

-- reg 66(1)(b). The amount of a benefit that counts as unearned income: nothing unless it is one of the listed benefits; then what is payable after
-- any adjustment for overlapping benefits; for carer support payment, no more than the carer's allowance you would get if entitled; for industrial
-- injuries benefit, less any increase under section 104 or 105; rounded to the penny.
@export How much of a benefit I receive counts as unearned income, in pounds (reg 66(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit is it?
      `what is payable to me after any overlapping benefits adjustment` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, is payable to you after any adjustment for overlapping benefits?
      `the carer's allowance I would receive if I were entitled` IS A NUMBER @desc How much carer's allowance, in pounds, would you receive if you were entitled to it? (0 if the benefit is not carer support payment)
      `the increase in industrial injuries benefit under section 104 or 105` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, is any increase in industrial injuries benefit under section 104 or 105 of the Contributions and Benefits Act? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of a benefit I receive counts as unearned income` IS
    `reg 66(1) — the amount of an item of income that counts as unearned income` `my benefit amount`
    WHERE
        `my benefit amount` MEANS `Amount of an item of income considered under regulation 66` WITH
            `item` IS `my benefit item`
            `amount payable after any overlapping benefits adjustment` IS `what is payable to me after any overlapping benefits adjustment`
            `amount of carer's allowance that a claimant would receive if entitled to it` IS `the carer's allowance I would receive if I were entitled`
            `increase in industrial injuries benefit under section 104 or 105` IS `the increase in industrial injuries benefit under section 104 or 105`
        `my benefit item` MEANS `Item of income considered under regulation 66` WITH
            `benefit to which the person is entitled` IS JUST `the benefit`
            -- This question is about a benefit only: the other ways an item of income can be unearned income are not asked here, and FALSE below means not asked. A benefit that is not listed in regulation 66(1)(b) counts for nothing.
            `retirement pension income to which the person is entitled` IS FALSE
            `benefit, allowance or other payment paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom and analogous to a benefit mentioned in sub-paragraph (b)` IS FALSE
            `payment towards the maintenance of the person by a spouse, civil partner, former spouse or former civil partner under a court order or an agreement for maintenance` IS FALSE
            `foreign state retirement pension` IS FALSE
            `student income` IS FALSE
            `payment under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973 or section 2 of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990` IS FALSE
            `payment is a substitute for universal credit` IS FALSE
            `payment is for a person's living expenses` IS FALSE
            `payment by a Sports Council named in section 23(2) of the National Lottery etc. Act 1993 out of sums allocated to it for distribution` IS FALSE
            `payment received under an insurance policy to insure against the risk of losing income due to illness, accident or redundancy` IS FALSE
            `income from an annuity` IS FALSE
            `income from an annuity is retirement pension income` IS FALSE
            `income from a trust` IS FALSE
            `income from an annuity or a trust is disregarded under regulation 75` IS FALSE
            `income from a trust is disregarded under regulation 76` IS FALSE
            `income treated as the yield from the person's capital by virtue of regulation 72` IS FALSE
            `capital treated as income by virtue of regulation 46(3) or (4)` IS FALSE
            `PPF periodic payments` IS FALSE
            `income taxable under Part 5 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 (miscellaneous income)` IS FALSE

-- reg 66(2)(a). A foreign state retirement pension is a pension paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom that is in the
-- nature of social security.
@export Is my pension from another country a foreign state retirement pension (reg 66(2)(a))?
GIVEN `it is paid under the law of another country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom?
      `it is in the nature of social security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in the nature of social security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my pension from another country a foreign state retirement pension` IF
    `reg 66(2)(a) — a foreign state retirement pension` `my pension`
    WHERE
        `my pension` MEANS `Pension that may be a foreign state retirement pension` WITH
            `paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom` IS `it is paid under the law of another country`
            `in the nature of social security` IS `it is in the nature of social security`

-- reg 66(2)(b). "Living expenses" are the cost of food, ordinary clothing or footwear, or household fuel, rent or other housing costs
-- (including council tax), for you, your partner, or a child or qualifying young person you are responsible for.
@export Is this cost a living expense (reg 66(2)(b))?
GIVEN `it is the cost of food` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the cost of food?
      `it is the cost of ordinary clothing or footwear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the cost of ordinary clothing or footwear?
      `it is the cost of household fuel, rent or other housing costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the cost of household fuel, rent or other housing costs (including council tax)?
      `it is for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for you?
      `it is for my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for your partner?
      `it is for a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for a child or qualifying young person for whom you are responsible?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this cost a living expense` IF
    `reg 66(2)(b) — living expenses` `this cost`
    WHERE
        `this cost` MEANS `Cost that may be a living expense` WITH
            `cost of food` IS `it is the cost of food`
            `cost of ordinary clothing or footwear` IS `it is the cost of ordinary clothing or footwear`
            `cost of household fuel, rent or other housing costs (including council tax)` IS `it is the cost of household fuel, rent or other housing costs`
            `for the person` IS `it is for me`
            `for the person's partner` IS `it is for my partner`
            `for a child or qualifying young person for whom the person is responsible` IS `it is for a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`

-- reg 67. Retirement pension income is retirement pension income within section 16 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002 as extended by
-- regulation 16 of the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002, and an increase in a Category A or B retirement pension for a partner.
@export Is my pension retirement pension income (reg 67)?
GIVEN `it is retirement pension income as the State Pension Credit rules define it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it retirement pension income within section 16 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002, as extended by regulation 16 of the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002?
      `it is an increase in a Category A or B retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an increase in a Category A or Category B retirement pension mentioned in section 16(1)(a) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002?
      `the increase is for my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the increase payable under Part 4 of the Contributions and Benefits Act in respect of your partner?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my pension retirement pension income` IF
    `reg 67 — retirement pension income` `my pension`
    WHERE
        `my pension` MEANS `Pension that may be retirement pension income` WITH
            `retirement pension income within section 16 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002 as extended by regulation 16 of the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002` IS `it is retirement pension income as the State Pension Credit rules define it`
            `increase in a Category A or Category B retirement pension mentioned in section 16(1)(a) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002` IS `it is an increase in a Category A or B retirement pension`
            `increase is payable under Part 4 of the Contributions and Benefits Act in respect of a person's partner` IS `the increase is for my partner`

-- reg 68(1). You are treated as having student income in an assessment period if you are undertaking a course and have, or are treated as
-- having, a loan or a grant for it, and the course (or its second or later year) begins in the period, or it is another period in which
-- you undertake the course (but not the long vacation or the period in which the course ends).
@export Am I treated as having student income in this assessment period (reg 68(1))?
GIVEN `I am undertaking a course of education, study or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undertaking a course of education, study or training?
      `I have a student loan for the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a student loan in respect of the course?
      `I have a postgraduate loan for the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a postgraduate loan in respect of the course?
      `I could get a student loan or postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could you acquire a student loan or postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps?
      `I have a grant for the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a grant in respect of the course?
      `the course begins in the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the course begin in the assessment period?
      `the course lasts two or more years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the course last two or more years?
      `the second or a later year of the course begins in the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the second or a later year of the course begin in the assessment period?
      `I undertake the course in the assessment period or part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you undertake the course in the assessment period, or in any part of it?
      `the long vacation begins in the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the long vacation begin in the assessment period?
      `the assessment period falls in the long vacation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assessment period fall within the long vacation?
      `the course ends in the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the course end in the assessment period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having student income in this assessment period` IF
    `reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` `my course`
    WHERE
        `my course` MEANS `Course and assessment period considered under regulation 68` WITH
            `undertaking a course of education, study or training` IS `I am undertaking a course of education, study or training`
            `student loan in respect of the course` IS `I have a student loan for the course`
            `postgraduate loan in respect of the course` IS `I have a postgraduate loan for the course`
            `could acquire a student loan or a postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps` IS `I could get a student loan or postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps`
            `grant in respect of the course` IS `I have a grant for the course`
            `the course begins in the assessment period` IS `the course begins in the assessment period`
            `the course lasts two or more years` IS `the course lasts two or more years`
            `the second or a subsequent year of the course begins in the assessment period` IS `the second or a later year of the course begins in the assessment period`
            `the person undertakes the course in the assessment period or in any part of it` IS `I undertake the course in the assessment period or part of it`
            `the long vacation begins in the assessment period` IS `the long vacation begins in the assessment period`
            `the assessment period falls within the long vacation` IS `the assessment period falls in the long vacation`
            `the course ends in the assessment period` IS `the course ends in the assessment period`

-- reg 68(2) to (4). Your student income is based on the amount of a loan if you have (or are treated as having) a student or
-- postgraduate loan; otherwise on the amount of a grant if you have one; otherwise there is nothing to base it on.
@export What is my student income based on: a loan, a grant or neither (reg 68(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `I have a student loan for the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a student loan in respect of the course?
      `I have a postgraduate loan for the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a postgraduate loan in respect of the course?
      `I could get a student loan or postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could you acquire a student loan or postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps?
      `I have a grant for the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a grant in respect of the course?
GIVETH A `Basis of student income`
DECIDE `What is my student income based on` IS
    `reg 68(2) to (4) — what the student income is based on` `my course`
    WHERE
        `my course` MEANS `Course and assessment period considered under regulation 68` WITH
            `student loan in respect of the course` IS `I have a student loan for the course`
            `postgraduate loan in respect of the course` IS `I have a postgraduate loan for the course`
            `could acquire a student loan or a postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps` IS `I could get a student loan or postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps`
            `grant in respect of the course` IS `I have a grant for the course`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `undertaking a course of education, study or training` IS FALSE
            `the course begins in the assessment period` IS FALSE
            `the course lasts two or more years` IS FALSE
            `the second or a subsequent year of the course begins in the assessment period` IS FALSE
            `the person undertakes the course in the assessment period or in any part of it` IS FALSE
            `the long vacation begins in the assessment period` IS FALSE
            `the assessment period falls within the long vacation` IS FALSE
            `the course ends in the assessment period` IS FALSE

-- reg 68(5). You are treated as having a student loan or postgraduate loan if you have one or could get one by taking reasonable steps.
@export Am I treated as having a student loan or a postgraduate loan (reg 68(5))?
GIVEN `I have a student loan for the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a student loan in respect of the course?
      `I have a postgraduate loan for the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a postgraduate loan in respect of the course?
      `I could get a student loan or postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could you acquire a student loan or postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having a student loan or a postgraduate loan` IF
    `reg 68(5) — the person is treated as having a student loan or a postgraduate loan` `my course`
    WHERE
        `my course` MEANS `Course and assessment period considered under regulation 68` WITH
            `student loan in respect of the course` IS `I have a student loan for the course`
            `postgraduate loan in respect of the course` IS `I have a postgraduate loan for the course`
            `could acquire a student loan or a postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps` IS `I could get a student loan or postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `undertaking a course of education, study or training` IS FALSE
            `grant in respect of the course` IS FALSE
            `the course begins in the assessment period` IS FALSE
            `the course lasts two or more years` IS FALSE
            `the second or a subsequent year of the course begins in the assessment period` IS FALSE
            `the person undertakes the course in the assessment period or in any part of it` IS FALSE
            `the long vacation begins in the assessment period` IS FALSE
            `the assessment period falls within the long vacation` IS FALSE
            `the course ends in the assessment period` IS FALSE

-- reg 68(6). A payment under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973 or section 2 of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990
-- that is referred to in regulation 66(1)(f) is not student income.
@export Does this payment count as student income (reg 68(6))?
GIVEN `it is a payment referred to in regulation 66(1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment referred to in regulation 66(1)(f) (a training allowance for living expenses, or one that replaces universal credit)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this payment count as student income` IF
    `reg 68(6) — a payment counts as student income` `it is a payment referred to in regulation 66(1)(f)`

-- reg 68(7). A "grant" is an educational grant or award of any kind, but not a student loan nor a payment under a scheme to enable persons
-- under 21 to complete courses that are not advanced education.
@export Is what I receive for my course a grant (reg 68(7))?
GIVEN `it is an educational grant or award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an educational grant or award of any kind?
      `it is a student loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a student loan?
      `it is a payment to help a person under 21 finish a course that is not advanced education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment under a scheme to enable persons under the age of 21 to complete courses of education or training that are not advanced education?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I receive for my course a grant` IF
    `reg 68(7) — grant` `my award`
    WHERE
        `my award` MEANS `Award that may be a grant` WITH
            `educational grant or award of any kind` IS `it is an educational grant or award`
            `student loan` IS `it is a student loan`
            `payment under a scheme to enable persons under the age of 21 to complete courses of education or training that are not advanced education` IS `it is a payment to help a person under 21 finish a course that is not advanced education`

-- reg 68(7). The "long vacation" is the longest vacation during a course intended to last two or more years, in the opinion of the
-- Secretary of State, if it lasts at least one month.
@export Is my vacation the long vacation (reg 68(7))?
GIVEN `the vacation starts on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the vacation start?
      `the vacation ends on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the vacation end?
      `the Secretary of State thinks it is the longest vacation of a course of two or more years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State of the opinion that it is the longest vacation during a course intended to last for two or more years?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my vacation the long vacation` IF
    `reg 68(7) — the long vacation` `the vacation starts on` `the vacation ends on` `the Secretary of State thinks it is the longest vacation of a course of two or more years`

-- reg 68(7). A "student loan" is a loan towards a student's maintenance pursuant to regulations under the Teaching and Higher Education Act 1998,
-- the Education (Scotland) Act 1980 or the Education (Student Support) (Northern Ireland) Order 1998.
@export Is my loan a student loan (reg 68(7))?
GIVEN `it is a loan towards my maintenance as a student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a loan towards your maintenance as a student?
      `it is made under the student support regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made pursuant to regulations under section 22 of the Teaching and Higher Education Act 1998, section 73 of the Education (Scotland) Act 1980 or Article 3 of the Education (Student Support) (Northern Ireland) Order 1998?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my loan a student loan` IF
    `reg 68(7) — student loan` `it is a loan towards my maintenance as a student` `it is made under the student support regulations`

-- reg 68(7). A "postgraduate loan" is a loan to a student on a postgraduate master's or doctoral degree course made pursuant to
-- regulations under section 22 of the Teaching and Higher Education Act 1998.
@export Is my loan a postgraduate loan (reg 68(7))?
GIVEN `it is a loan for a postgraduate master's or doctoral course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a loan to a student undertaking a postgraduate master's or doctoral degree course?
      `it is made under regulations under section 22 of the 1998 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made pursuant to regulations made under section 22 of the Teaching and Higher Education Act 1998?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my loan a postgraduate loan` IF
    `reg 68(7) — postgraduate loan` `it is a loan for a postgraduate master's or doctoral course` `it is made under regulations under section 22 of the 1998 Act`

-- reg 69(1). The student loan taken into account is the maximum you could be paid for the year (with increases for additional weeks),
-- assuming no reduction on account of means or of any grant.
@export How much of my student loan is taken into account, in pounds (reg 69(1))?
GIVEN `the most the student loan could be for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum student loan, in pounds, for the year, with increases for additional weeks, assuming no reduction on account of means or of any grant?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my student loan is taken into account` IS
    `reg 69(1) — the amount of a student loan taken into account` `the most the student loan could be for the year`

-- reg 69(1A). 30% of the maximum postgraduate loan is taken into account, assuming no reduction on account of means or of any grant.
@export How much of my postgraduate loan is taken into account, in pounds (reg 69(1A))?
GIVEN `the most the postgraduate loan could be` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum postgraduate loan, in pounds, assuming no reduction on account of means or of any grant?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my postgraduate loan is taken into account` IS
    `reg 69(1A) — the amount of a postgraduate loan taken into account` `the most the postgraduate loan could be`

-- reg 70. The grant taken into account is the whole grant less the payments for tuition and examination fees, for disability, for
-- additional term-time residential costs, for maintaining a home elsewhere (unless your award includes housing costs for it), for another person's
-- maintenance (unless your award includes an amount for them), for books and equipment, for travel and for childcare.
@export How much of my grant is taken into account, in pounds (reg 70)?
GIVEN `the whole of my grant` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the whole grant, in pounds?
      `of which for tuition or examination fees` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, is intended to meet tuition fees or examination fees?
      `of which for my disability` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, is in respect of your disability?
      `of which for living away during term time` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, is intended to meet additional expenditure connected with term-time residential study away from your educational establishment?
      `of which for keeping a second home` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, is intended to meet the cost of maintaining a home elsewhere than where you live during your course?
      `my award includes housing costs for that home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your award of universal credit include the housing costs element for those costs?
      `of which for another person's maintenance` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, is intended for the maintenance of another person?
      `my award includes an amount for that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your award of universal credit include an amount in respect of that other person?
      `of which for books and equipment` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, is intended to meet the cost of books and equipment?
      `of which for travel` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, is intended to meet travel expenses of attending the course?
      `of which for childcare` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that, how much, in pounds, is intended to meet childcare costs?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my grant is taken into account` IS
    `reg 70 — the amount of a grant taken into account` `my grant`
    WHERE
        `my grant` MEANS `Grant counted as student income` WITH
            `whole of the grant` IS `the whole of my grant`
            `payment intended to meet tuition fees or examination fees` IS `of which for tuition or examination fees`
            `payment in respect of the person's disability` IS `of which for my disability`
            `payment intended to meet additional expenditure connected with term time residential study away from the person's educational establishment` IS `of which for living away during term time`
            `payment intended to meet the cost of the person maintaining a home at a place other than that at which they reside during their course` IS `of which for keeping a second home`
            `an award of universal credit includes the housing costs element in respect of those costs` IS `my award includes housing costs for that home`
            `payment intended for the maintenance of another person` IS `of which for another person's maintenance`
            `an award of universal credit includes an amount in respect of that other person` IS `my award includes an amount for that person`
            `payment intended to meet the cost of books and equipment` IS `of which for books and equipment`
            `payment intended to meet travel expenses incurred as a result of the person's attendance on the course` IS `of which for travel`
            `payment intended to meet childcare costs` IS `of which for childcare`

-- reg 68(3). Where your student income is based on a loan, any grant for the same period is disregarded, except a specific amount in the grant to cover
-- rent payments for which your award includes the housing costs element, and any amount intended for the maintenance of another person for whom your
-- award includes an amount. This is the part of the grant that still counts.
@export How much of my grant still counts when my student income is based on a loan, in pounds (reg 68(3))?
GIVEN `the amount in my grant to cover rent that my award includes the housing costs element for` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the grant, in pounds, is a specific amount to cover rent payments for which an amount is included in your award of universal credit for the housing costs element?
      `the amount in my grant for another person whom my award includes an amount for` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the grant, in pounds, is intended for the maintenance of another person for whom an amount is included in your award of universal credit?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my grant still counts when I have a student loan` IS
    `reg 68(3) — the part of a grant that is not disregarded when student income is based on a loan` `the amount in my grant to cover rent that my award includes the housing costs element for` `the amount in my grant for another person whom my award includes an amount for`

-- reg 71. Student income for an assessment period: the loan (and the part of any grant not disregarded) or the grant, for the year or the
-- course if shorter, divided by the number of assessment periods (and earlier months) over which it is spread, less 110 pounds. The seat
-- asks the basis as the three choices of reg 68(2) to (4). Where there are no assessment periods the answer is "nothing", not covered.
@export What is my student income for an assessment period, in pounds (reg 71)?
GIVEN `what my student income is based on` IS A `Basis of student income` @desc What is your student income based on?
      `my student loan for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your student loan, in pounds, for the year of the course (or for the course if it is shorter)? (0 if none)
      `my postgraduate loan for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your postgraduate loan, in pounds, for the year of the course (or for the course if it is shorter)? (0 if none)
      `the part of my grant that counts` IS A NUMBER @desc What part of any grant, in pounds, is not disregarded? (0 if none)
      `my grant for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your grant, in pounds, for the year of the course (or for the course if it is shorter)? (0 if none)
      `I have a student loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a student loan?
      `I have a postgraduate loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a postgraduate loan?
      `the number of assessment periods the income is spread over` IS A NUMBER @desc Over how many assessment periods in the year (or course) are you treated as having student income?
      `the earlier months before my award` IS A NUMBER @desc How many earlier months of one month each, beginning on the same day as the assessment periods, precede the start of your award and fall in that year or course?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my student income for an assessment period` IS
    `reg 71 — the student income for an assessment period` `my student income`
    WHERE
        `my student income` MEANS `Student income for an assessment period` WITH
            `basis` IS `what my student income is based on`
            `student loan for the year of the course, or for the course if it is shorter` IS `my student loan for the year`
            `postgraduate loan for the year of the course, or for the course if it is shorter` IS `my postgraduate loan for the year`
            `part of any grant that is not disregarded` IS `the part of my grant that counts`
            `grant for the year of the course, or for the course if it is shorter` IS `my grant for the year`
            `person has a student loan` IS `I have a student loan`
            `person has a postgraduate loan` IS `I have a postgraduate loan`
            `assessment periods in the year of the course, or in the course if it is shorter, for which the person is treated as having student income` IS `the number of assessment periods the income is spread over`
            `earlier months of one month each, beginning on the same day as the assessment periods, that precede the commencement of the award and fall in that year of the course or that course` IS `the earlier months before my award`

-- reg 72(1). Your capital over 6,000 pounds is treated as yielding a monthly income of 4.35 pounds for each 250 pounds (or part of 250) above 6,000.
@export How much monthly income is my capital treated as yielding, in pounds (reg 72(1))?
GIVEN `my capital` IS A NUMBER @desc How much capital do you have, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much monthly income is my capital treated as yielding` IS
    `reg 72(1) — the monthly income that capital is treated as yielding` `my capital`

-- reg 72(2). The yield in reg 72(1) is not applied to capital that is disregarded, or whose actual income is taken into account as income
-- from an annuity or a trust.
@export Is my capital treated as yielding income (reg 72(2))?
GIVEN `the capital is left out of the count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the capital disregarded (see the questions about Schedule 10 and regulations 75 to 77)?
      `its actual income counts as income from an annuity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the actual income from the capital taken into account under regulation 66(1)(i) (income from an annuity)?
      `its actual income counts as income from a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the actual income from the capital taken into account under regulation 66(1)(j) (income from a trust)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my capital treated as yielding income` IF
    `reg 72(2) — paragraph (1) applies to the capital` `the capital is left out of the count` `its actual income counts as income from an annuity` `its actual income counts as income from a trust`

-- reg 72(3). The actual income from capital that is treated as yielding income counts as part of the capital from the day it is due to be
-- paid to you.
@export Is the actual income from my capital treated as part of my capital (reg 72(3))?
GIVEN `my capital is treated as yielding income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the capital treated as yielding income (see the question about regulation 72(2))?
      `the day the actual income is due to be paid to me` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the actual income due to be paid to you?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the actual income from my capital treated as part of my capital` IF
    `reg 72(3) — the actual income derived from the capital is treated as part of the capital` `my capital is treated as yielding income` `the day the actual income is due to be paid to me` `the day my capital is being worked out`

-- reg 73(2). Unearned income paid weekly, two-weekly, four-weekly, three-monthly or annually is brought to a monthly equivalent (monthly
-- unchanged).
@export What is the monthly equivalent of my unearned income, in pounds (reg 73(2))?
GIVEN `the amount I am paid each time` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, are you paid each time?
      `how often I am paid` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often are you paid?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the monthly equivalent of my unearned income` IS
    `reg 73(2) — the monthly equivalent of a payment of unearned income` `the amount I am paid each time` `how often I am paid`

-- reg 73(2A). The amount of unearned income for the assessment period is the monthly amount (or equivalent), unless the period it is paid
-- for begins or ends during the assessment period; in that case the formula for the number of days in the source is missing from the
-- converted text and the answer is "not covered" (NOTHING).
@export How much of my unearned income counts in this assessment period, in pounds (reg 73(2A))?
GIVEN `the period it is paid for begins or ends in this assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the period for which the unearned income is paid begin or end during the assessment period?
      `the days of it that fall in this assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of that period fall within the assessment period?
      `the monthly amount` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the monthly amount (or monthly equivalent), in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my unearned income counts in this assessment period` IS
    `reg 73(2A) — the amount of unearned income for the assessment period` `the period it is paid for begins or ends in this assessment period` `the days of it that fall in this assessment period` `the monthly amount`

-- reg 73(3). Unearned income that fluctuates is averaged over its identifiable cycle, or otherwise over the period that gives the
-- more accurate monthly equivalent (3 months if no better period is stated).
@export What is the monthly equivalent of my fluctuating unearned income, in pounds (reg 73(3))?
GIVEN `the total I received over the cycle or period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much unearned income, in pounds, did you receive in total over the cycle or the period?
      `there is an identifiable cycle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an identifiable cycle?
      `the cycle lasts this many months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many months does the cycle last? (0 if none)
      `a better period would give a more accurate monthly figure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, is there another period that would let the monthly equivalent be worked out more accurately?
      `that other period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many months is it? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the monthly equivalent of my fluctuating unearned income` IS
    `reg 73(3) — the monthly equivalent of unearned income that fluctuates` `my fluctuating income`
    WHERE
        `my fluctuating income` MEANS `Fluctuating unearned income` WITH
            `total unearned income received over the cycle or the period` IS `the total I received over the cycle or period`
            `there is an identifiable cycle` IS `there is an identifiable cycle`
            `duration of the identifiable cycle in months` IS `the cycle lasts this many months`
            `other period in months that would enable the monthly equivalent to be determined more accurately` IS IF `a better period would give a more accurate monthly figure` THEN JUST `that other period in months` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 73(4). Regulation 73 does not apply to student income.
@export Does the monthly calculation of regulation 73 apply to my income (reg 73(4))?
GIVEN `the income is student income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the income student income?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the monthly calculation of regulation 73 apply to my income` IF
    `reg 73(4) — regulation 73 applies to the income` `the income is student income`

-- reg 74(1). You are treated as having unearned income that would be available to you if you applied for it, other than the benefits listed in
-- regulation 66(1)(b).
@export Am I treated as having income that I could get by applying for it (reg 74(1))?
GIVEN `the income would be available to me if I applied for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would unearned income be available to you upon the making of an application for it?
      `it is a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the income a benefit?
      `the benefit` IS A Benefit @desc If so, which benefit? (any, if the answer above is no)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having income that I could get by applying for it` IF
    `reg 74(1) — the person is treated as having unearned income that would be available on application` `the income would be available to me if I applied for it` (IF `it is a benefit` THEN JUST `the benefit` ELSE NOTHING)

-- reg 74(3). If you have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit and have not applied for retirement pension income, you are
-- treated as having the retirement pension income you might expect to be entitled to if you claimed.
@export What retirement pension income am I treated as having if I have not applied for it, in pounds (reg 74(3))?
GIVEN `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the qualifying age for state pension credit?
      `I have not applied for the pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not applied for the retirement pension income?
      `the pension I might expect if I claimed` IS A NUMBER @desc What retirement pension income, in pounds, might you expect to be entitled to if you made a claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What retirement pension income am I treated as having if I have not applied for it` IS
    `reg 74(3) — the retirement pension income the person is treated as possessing` `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` `I have not applied for the pension` `the pension I might expect if I claimed`

-- reg 74(4). You are treated as possessing retirement pension income in the circumstances in which regulation 18 of the State Pension
-- Credit Regulations 2002 treats a person as receiving it for state pension credit.
@export Am I treated as possessing retirement pension income as for state pension credit (reg 74(4))?
GIVEN `regulation 18 of the State Pension Credit Regulations treats me as receiving it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances those in which regulation 18 of the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002 treats a person as receiving retirement pension income for state pension credit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as possessing retirement pension income as for state pension credit` IF
    `reg 74(4) — the person is treated as possessing retirement pension income` `regulation 18 of the State Pension Credit Regulations treats me as receiving it`


§§ `Part 6, Chapter 4 -- Miscellaneous (regulations 75 to 77)`

-- reg 75(2). Regular payments of a sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury are disregarded in calculating your unearned income.
@export Are the regular payments of my personal injury compensation left out of my unearned income (reg 75(2))?
GIVEN `the sum was awarded or agreed because of a personal injury to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the sum awarded to you, or agreed by or on behalf of you, in consequence of a personal injury to you?
      `I receive the sum as regular payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under an order of the court or an agreement, do you receive all or part of the sum by way of regular payments?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the regular payments of my personal injury compensation left out of my unearned income` IF
    `reg 75(2) — the regular payments are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income` `my sum`
    WHERE
        `my sum` MEANS `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury` WITH
            `sum awarded to the person, or agreed by or on behalf of the person, in consequence of a personal injury to that person` IS `the sum was awarded or agreed because of a personal injury to me`
            `in accordance with an order of the court or an agreement, the person receives all or part of the sum by way of regular payments` IS `I receive the sum as regular payments`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the sum has been used to purchase an annuity` IS FALSE
            `the sum is held in trust` IS FALSE
            `the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person or can only be disposed of by direction of the court` IS FALSE
            `the sum has otherwise been disposed of` IS FALSE
            `date on which the sum was paid to the person` IS NOTHING

-- reg 75(3). Annuity payments bought with a sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury are disregarded in calculating your unearned income.
@export Are the annuity payments bought with my personal injury compensation left out of my unearned income (reg 75(3))?
GIVEN `the sum was awarded or agreed because of a personal injury to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the sum awarded to you, or agreed by or on behalf of you, in consequence of a personal injury to you?
      `the sum was used to buy an annuity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sum been used to purchase an annuity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the annuity payments bought with my personal injury compensation left out of my unearned income` IF
    `reg 75(3) — the annuity payments are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income` `my sum`
    WHERE
        `my sum` MEANS `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury` WITH
            `sum awarded to the person, or agreed by or on behalf of the person, in consequence of a personal injury to that person` IS `the sum was awarded or agreed because of a personal injury to me`
            `the sum has been used to purchase an annuity` IS `the sum was used to buy an annuity`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `in accordance with an order of the court or an agreement, the person receives all or part of the sum by way of regular payments` IS FALSE
            `the sum is held in trust` IS FALSE
            `the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person or can only be disposed of by direction of the court` IS FALSE
            `the sum has otherwise been disposed of` IS FALSE
            `date on which the sum was paid to the person` IS NOTHING

-- reg 75(4). Where the sum is held in trust, the capital of the trust and the income from it are disregarded.
@export Is my personal injury compensation held in trust left out of my capital and income (reg 75(4))?
GIVEN `the sum was awarded or agreed because of a personal injury to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the sum awarded to you, or agreed by or on behalf of you, in consequence of a personal injury to you?
      `the sum is held in trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sum held in trust?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my personal injury compensation held in trust left out of my capital and income` IF
    `reg 75(4) — the capital of the trust or the income from it is disregarded` `my sum`
    WHERE
        `my sum` MEANS `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury` WITH
            `sum awarded to the person, or agreed by or on behalf of the person, in consequence of a personal injury to that person` IS `the sum was awarded or agreed because of a personal injury to me`
            `the sum is held in trust` IS `the sum is held in trust`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `in accordance with an order of the court or an agreement, the person receives all or part of the sum by way of regular payments` IS FALSE
            `the sum has been used to purchase an annuity` IS FALSE
            `the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person or can only be disposed of by direction of the court` IS FALSE
            `the sum has otherwise been disposed of` IS FALSE
            `date on which the sum was paid to the person` IS NOTHING

-- reg 75(5). Where the sum is administered by the court on your behalf or can only be disposed of by direction of the court, the sum and the
-- regular payments from it are disregarded.
@export Is my personal injury compensation administered by the court left out of my capital and income (reg 75(5))?
GIVEN `the sum was awarded or agreed because of a personal injury to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the sum awarded to you, or agreed by or on behalf of you, in consequence of a personal injury to you?
      `the court administers the sum for me or must direct its use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sum administered by the court on your behalf, or can it only be disposed of by direction of the court?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my personal injury compensation administered by the court left out of my capital and income` IF
    `reg 75(5) — the sum or the regular payments from it are disregarded` `my sum`
    WHERE
        `my sum` MEANS `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury` WITH
            `sum awarded to the person, or agreed by or on behalf of the person, in consequence of a personal injury to that person` IS `the sum was awarded or agreed because of a personal injury to me`
            `the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person or can only be disposed of by direction of the court` IS `the court administers the sum for me or must direct its use`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `in accordance with an order of the court or an agreement, the person receives all or part of the sum by way of regular payments` IS FALSE
            `the sum has been used to purchase an annuity` IS FALSE
            `the sum is held in trust` IS FALSE
            `the sum has otherwise been disposed of` IS FALSE
            `date on which the sum was paid to the person` IS NOTHING

-- reg 75(6). The sum is disregarded in calculating your capital for 12 months from the day it was paid to you, unless it is held in
-- trust, has been used for an annuity, or has otherwise been disposed of.
@export Is my personal injury compensation left out of my capital for now (reg 75(6))?
GIVEN `the sum was awarded or agreed because of a personal injury to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the sum awarded to you, or agreed by or on behalf of you, in consequence of a personal injury to you?
      `the sum is held in trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sum held in trust?
      `the sum was used to buy an annuity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sum been used to purchase an annuity?
      `the sum has been disposed of in some other way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sum otherwise been disposed of?
      `the day the sum was paid to me` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the sum paid to you?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my personal injury compensation left out of my capital for now` IF
    `reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` `my sum` `the day my capital is being worked out`
    WHERE
        `my sum` MEANS `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury` WITH
            `sum awarded to the person, or agreed by or on behalf of the person, in consequence of a personal injury to that person` IS `the sum was awarded or agreed because of a personal injury to me`
            `the sum has been used to purchase an annuity` IS `the sum was used to buy an annuity`
            `the sum is held in trust` IS `the sum is held in trust`
            `the sum has otherwise been disposed of` IS `the sum has been disposed of in some other way`
            `date on which the sum was paid to the person` IS JUST `the day the sum was paid to me`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `in accordance with an order of the court or an agreement, the person receives all or part of the sum by way of regular payments` IS FALSE
            `the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person or can only be disposed of by direction of the court` IS FALSE

-- reg 76. A payment is disregarded, whether capital or income, if it comes from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose
-- (reg 76(1)); from one of the listed bodies or schemes (reg 76(1A)); for the Grenfell Tower fire (reg 76(1B)); is a vaccine damage payment, or
-- derives from one (reg 76(1C)); is a miscarriage of justice compensation payment, or derives from one (reg 76(1D)); and a payment from the
-- scheme or trust that state pension credit would disregard is disregarded for a claim by someone other than the person with the disease or
-- infection (reg 76(3)). The one question asks all of the facts, and answers "no" if none of them applies.
@export Is a special compensation payment I received left out of my capital and income (reg 76)?
GIVEN `the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment from a scheme established or approved by the Secretary of State, or from a trust established with funds provided by the Secretary of State?
      `it is for people with variant CJD or infected blood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its purpose compensation or support for a person diagnosed with variant Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease or infected from contaminated blood products?
      `it is for the bombings in London on 7 July 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its purpose compensation or support in respect of the bombings in London on 7th July 2005?
      `it is for people interned or harmed in the Second World War` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its purpose compensation or support for persons who were interned or suffered forced labour, injury, property loss or loss of a child during the Second World War?
      `it is for the London terrorist attacks of 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its purpose compensation or support in respect of the terrorist attacks in London on 22nd March 2017 or 3rd June 2017?
      `it is for the Manchester bombing of 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its purpose compensation or support in respect of the bombing in Manchester on 22nd May 2017?
      `it is for historic institutional child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its purpose compensation or support in respect of historic institutional child abuse in the United Kingdom?
      `it is to help a disabled person live independently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its purpose supporting persons with a disability to live independently in their accommodation?
      `it is from the National Emergencies Trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from the National Emergencies Trust (registered charity number 1182809)?
      `it is from the Child Migrants Trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from the Child Migrants Trust (registered charity number 1171479) under the scheme for former British child migrants?
      `it is from the Windrush Compensation Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from the scheme established by the Windrush Compensation Scheme (Expenditure) Act 2020?
      `it is from the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the Horizon failings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from the Post Office or the Secretary of State to provide compensation or support in connection with the failings of the Horizon system?
      `it is from the Post Office or the Secretary of State following the Bates judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from the Post Office or the Secretary of State to provide compensation or support otherwise payable following the judgment in Bates and Others v Post Office Ltd (No. 3) (Common Issues)?
      `it is from the Victims of Overseas Terrorism Compensation Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from the Victims of Overseas Terrorism Compensation Scheme established by the Ministry of Justice in 2012?
      `it is from the LGBT Financial Recognition Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from the Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual and Transgender Financial Recognition Scheme?
      `it is for the Grenfell Tower fire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made to provide compensation or support in respect of the fire on 14th June 2017 at Grenfell Tower?
      `I receive a vaccine damage payment, or one is made for my benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a vaccine damage payment, or is one made for your benefit?
      `I am the partner of someone who got a vaccine damage payment and receive a payment derived from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the partner of a person who receives a vaccine damage payment, and do you receive a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from it?
      `I was the partner of a person who got a vaccine damage payment and receive a payment from their estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you the partner of a person who received a vaccine damage payment, immediately before their death, and do you receive a payment from their estate which is derived from it?
      `a vaccine damage payment went to the personal representative of my late partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a vaccine damage payment made to the personal representative of a person who was severely disabled as a result of vaccination, and were you their partner immediately before their death, and do you receive a payment from their estate which is derived from it?
      `I receive a miscarriage of justice compensation payment, or one is made for my benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a miscarriage of justice compensation payment, or is one made for your benefit?
      `I am the partner of someone who got a miscarriage of justice payment and receive a payment derived from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the partner of a person who receives a miscarriage of justice compensation payment, and do you receive a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from it?
      `I was the partner of a person who got a miscarriage of justice payment and receive a payment from their estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you the partner of a person who received a miscarriage of justice compensation payment, immediately before their death, and do you receive a payment from their estate which is derived from it?
      `a miscarriage of justice payment went to the personal representative of my late partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a miscarriage of justice compensation payment made to the personal representative of a deceased person, and were you their partner immediately before their death, and do you receive a payment from their estate which is derived from it?
      `the payment is capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment capital?
      `the claim is made by someone other than the person with the disease or infection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim made by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person referred to in regulation 76(1)(a)(i)?
      `state pension credit would leave it out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment received from the scheme or trust, or derived from a payment from it, and would it be disregarded for state pension credit by virtue of paragraph 13 or 15 of Schedule 5 to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a special compensation payment I received left out of my capital and income` IF
    `reg 76 — the payment is disregarded in the calculation of capital or income` `my payment`
    WHERE
        `my payment` MEANS `Payment considered under regulation 76` WITH
            `payment from a scheme established or approved by the Secretary of State, or from a trust established with funds provided by the Secretary of State` IS `the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State`
            `purpose: compensation or support for a person diagnosed with variant Creutzfeldt-Jacob disease or infected from contaminated blood products` IS `it is for people with variant CJD or infected blood`
            `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the bombings in London on 7th July 2005` IS `it is for the bombings in London on 7 July 2005`
            `purpose: compensation or support for persons who have been interned or suffered forced labour, injury, property loss or loss of a child during the Second World War` IS `it is for people interned or harmed in the Second World War`
            `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the terrorist attacks in London on 22nd March 2017 or 3rd June 2017` IS `it is for the London terrorist attacks of 2017`
            `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the bombing in Manchester on 22nd May 2017` IS `it is for the Manchester bombing of 2017`
            `purpose: compensation or support in respect of historic institutional child abuse in the United Kingdom` IS `it is for historic institutional child abuse`
            `purpose: supporting persons with a disability to live independently in their accommodation` IS `it is to help a disabled person live independently`
            `payment from the National Emergencies Trust, registered charity number 1182809` IS `it is from the National Emergencies Trust`
            `payment from the Child Migrants Trust, registered charity number 1171479, under the scheme for former British child migrants` IS `it is from the Child Migrants Trust`
            `payment from the scheme established by the Windrush Compensation Scheme (Expenditure) Act 2020` IS `it is from the Windrush Compensation Scheme`
            `payment from the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the purpose of providing compensation or support in connection with the failings of the Horizon system` IS `it is from the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the Horizon failings`
            `payment from the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the purpose of providing compensation or support otherwise payable following the judgment in Bates and Others v Post Office Ltd (No. 3) (Common Issues)` IS `it is from the Post Office or the Secretary of State following the Bates judgment`
            `payment from the Victims of Overseas Terrorism Compensation Scheme established by the Ministry of Justice in 2012 under section 47 of the Crime and Security Act 2010` IS `it is from the Victims of Overseas Terrorism Compensation Scheme`
            `payment from the Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual and Transgender Financial Recognition Scheme administered under the authority of the Secretary of State for Defence` IS `it is from the LGBT Financial Recognition Scheme`
            `payment made for the purpose of providing compensation or support in respect of the fire on 14th June 2017 at Grenfell Tower` IS `it is for the Grenfell Tower fire`
            `the person receives a vaccine damage payment or is a person for whose benefit a vaccine damage payment is made` IS `I receive a vaccine damage payment, or one is made for my benefit`
            `the person is the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1C)(a) and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from a vaccine damage payment` IS `I am the partner of someone who got a vaccine damage payment and receive a payment derived from it`
            `the person was the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1C)(a) immediately before the latter's death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment` IS `I was the partner of a person who got a vaccine damage payment and receive a payment from their estate`
            `a vaccine damage payment is made to the personal representative of a person who was severely disabled as a result of vaccination (P), and the person was P's partner immediately before P's death and receives a payment from P's estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment` IS `a vaccine damage payment went to the personal representative of my late partner`
            `the person receives a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or is a person for whose benefit such a payment is made` IS `I receive a miscarriage of justice compensation payment, or one is made for my benefit`
            `the person is the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1D)(a) and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment` IS `I am the partner of someone who got a miscarriage of justice payment and receive a payment derived from it`
            `the person was the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1D)(a) immediately before their death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a miscarriage of justice compensation payment` IS `I was the partner of a person who got a miscarriage of justice payment and receive a payment from their estate`
            `a miscarriage of justice compensation payment is made to the personal representative of a deceased person (P), and the person was P's partner immediately before P's death and receives a payment from P's estate which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment` IS `a miscarriage of justice payment went to the personal representative of my late partner`
            `the payment is capital` IS `the payment is capital`
            `the claim is made by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person referred to in regulation 76(1)(a)(i)` IS `the claim is made by someone other than the person with the disease or infection`
            `the payment is received from the scheme or trust, or derives from a payment received from it, and would be disregarded in relation to an award of state pension credit by virtue of paragraph 13 or 15 of Schedule 5 to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002` IS `state pension credit would leave it out`

-- reg 76(4). A "miscarriage of justice compensation payment" is a payment under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988, or one made by the
-- Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or (in Northern Ireland) the Department of Justice to compensate for a miscarriage of justice in criminal
-- proceedings or for being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence.
@export Is the payment I received a miscarriage of justice compensation payment (reg 76(4))?
GIVEN `it is a payment under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment made under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988?
      `it is paid by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or the Department of Justice in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or, in Northern Ireland, the Department of Justice?
      `it compensates a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made for the purpose of compensating a person for a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings?
      `it compensates being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made for the purpose of compensating a person for being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the payment I received a miscarriage of justice compensation payment` IF
    `reg 76(4) — miscarriage of justice compensation payment` `my payment`
    WHERE
        `my payment` MEANS `Payment that may be a miscarriage of justice compensation payment` WITH
            `payment made under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988` IS `it is a payment under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988`
            `payment made by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or, in Northern Ireland, the Department of Justice` IS `it is paid by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or the Department of Justice in Northern Ireland`
            `made for the purpose of compensating a person for a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings` IS `it compensates a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings`
            `made for the purpose of compensating a person for being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence` IS `it compensates being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence`

-- reg 77(1), (5). A person in a position analogous to a sole owner or partner of a company carrying on a trade or a property business is
-- treated as a sole owner or partner, unless the income they derive from the company is employed earnings by virtue of Chapters 8 to 10 of Part 2 of
-- ITEPA derived from their main employment.
@export Am I treated as the sole owner or a partner of my company (reg 77(1), (5))?
GIVEN `I stand in the position of a sole owner or partner of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you stand in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company?
      `the company carries on a trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company carrying on a trade?
      `the company carries on a property business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company carrying on a property business?
      `I am paid through an intermediary for work that is my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you derive income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA (for example, through an intermediary)?
      `that income is from my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that income derived from activities that are your main employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as the sole owner or a partner of my company` IF
    `reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` `my company`
    WHERE
        `my company` MEANS `Person in relation to a company` WITH
            `the person stands in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company` IS `I stand in the position of a sole owner or partner of the company`
            `the company is carrying on a trade` IS `the company carries on a trade`
            `the company is carrying on a property business` IS `the company carries on a property business`
            `the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA` IS `I am paid through an intermediary for work that is my main employment`
            `that income is derived from activities that are the person's main employment` IS `that income is from my main employment`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `value of the capital of the company` IS 0
            `fraction of the value that is the person's share` IS NOTHING
            `value of any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade` IS 0
            `the person is engaged in activities in the course of that trade` IS FALSE
            `the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment` IS FALSE
            `the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having by virtue of paragraph (3)(b)` IS `the company's earnings placeholder`
            `employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee of the company` IS 0
        `the company's earnings placeholder` MEANS `Self-employed earnings considered under regulation 57` WITH
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `trades, professions or vocations carried on by the person in the assessment period` IS EMPTY
            `payments made by the person to HMRC in the assessment period by way of national insurance contributions or income tax in respect of any trade, profession or vocation` IS 0
            `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period` IS 0
            `a deduction has been made in respect of those contributions in calculating the person's employed earnings` IS FALSE
            `unused losses, oldest first` IS EMPTY

-- reg 77(2), (3)(a). The person is treated as possessing the company's capital (or their share of it), less the value of the assets used
-- wholly and exclusively for the trade if the person is engaged in the trade; the holding itself is then disregarded.
@export How much of my company's capital am I treated as possessing, in pounds (reg 77(2), (3)(a))?
GIVEN `I stand in the position of a sole owner or partner of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you stand in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company?
      `the company carries on a trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company carrying on a trade?
      `the company carries on a property business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company carrying on a property business?
      `the company is worth` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value, in pounds, of the capital of the company?
      `my share of the company is a stated fraction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your share of the company a fraction that you can state?
      `my share of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what fraction of the value is your share? (for example 0.5 for a half; 0 if not stated)
      `the company's trading assets are worth` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value, in pounds, of the assets of the company used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade?
      `I work in the trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you engaged in activities in the course of that trade?
      `the trade is my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your activities in the course of the trade your main employment?
      `I am paid through an intermediary for work that is my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you derive income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA (for example, through an intermediary)?
      `that income is from my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that income derived from activities that are your main employment?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my company's capital am I treated as possessing` IS
    `reg 77(2) — the capital the person is treated as possessing` `my company`
    WHERE
        `my company` MEANS `Person in relation to a company` WITH
            `the person stands in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company` IS `I stand in the position of a sole owner or partner of the company`
            `the company is carrying on a trade` IS `the company carries on a trade`
            `the company is carrying on a property business` IS `the company carries on a property business`
            `value of the capital of the company` IS `the company is worth`
            `fraction of the value that is the person's share` IS IF `my share of the company is a stated fraction` THEN JUST `my share of the company` ELSE NOTHING
            `value of any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade` IS `the company's trading assets are worth`
            `the person is engaged in activities in the course of that trade` IS `I work in the trade`
            `the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment` IS `the trade is my main employment`
            `the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA` IS `I am paid through an intermediary for work that is my main employment`
            `that income is derived from activities that are the person's main employment` IS `that income is from my main employment`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having by virtue of paragraph (3)(b)` IS `the company's earnings placeholder`
            `employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee of the company` IS 0
        `the company's earnings placeholder` MEANS `Self-employed earnings considered under regulation 57` WITH
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `trades, professions or vocations carried on by the person in the assessment period` IS EMPTY
            `payments made by the person to HMRC in the assessment period by way of national insurance contributions or income tax in respect of any trade, profession or vocation` IS 0
            `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period` IS 0
            `a deduction has been made in respect of those contributions in calculating the person's employed earnings` IS FALSE
            `unused losses, oldest first` IS EMPTY

-- reg 77(2). Where regulation 77(1) applies, the value of the person's holding in the company is disregarded: they are treated as possessing the
-- company's capital (or their share of it) instead.
@export Is the value of my holding in my company disregarded (reg 77(2))?
GIVEN `I stand in the position of a sole owner or partner of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you stand in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company?
      `the company carries on a trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company carrying on a trade?
      `the company carries on a property business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company carrying on a property business?
      `I am paid through an intermediary for work that is my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you derive income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA (for example, through an intermediary)?
      `that income is from my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that income derived from activities that are your main employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the value of my holding in my company disregarded` IF
    `reg 77(2) — the value of the person's holding in the company is disregarded` `my company`
    WHERE
        `my company` MEANS `Person in relation to a company` WITH
            `the person stands in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company` IS `I stand in the position of a sole owner or partner of the company`
            `the company is carrying on a trade` IS `the company carries on a trade`
            `the company is carrying on a property business` IS `the company carries on a property business`
            `the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA` IS `I am paid through an intermediary for work that is my main employment`
            `that income is derived from activities that are the person's main employment` IS `that income is from my main employment`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `value of the capital of the company` IS 0
            `fraction of the value that is the person's share` IS NOTHING
            `value of any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade` IS 0
            `the person is engaged in activities in the course of that trade` IS FALSE
            `the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment` IS FALSE
            `the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having by virtue of paragraph (3)(b)` IS `the company's earnings placeholder`
            `employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee of the company` IS 0
        `the company's earnings placeholder` MEANS `Self-employed earnings considered under regulation 57` WITH
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `trades, professions or vocations carried on by the person in the assessment period` IS EMPTY
            `payments made by the person to HMRC in the assessment period by way of national insurance contributions or income tax in respect of any trade, profession or vocation` IS 0
            `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period` IS 0
            `a deduction has been made in respect of those contributions in calculating the person's employed earnings` IS FALSE
            `unused losses, oldest first` IS EMPTY

-- reg 77(3)(c). A person treated under regulation 77(1) as a sole owner or partner of a company carrying on a trade, whose activities in the trade
-- are their main employment, is treated as being in gainful self-employment, so that regulation 62 applies.
@export Am I treated as being in gainful self-employment through my company (reg 77(3)(c))?
GIVEN `I stand in the position of a sole owner or partner of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you stand in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company?
      `the company carries on a trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company carrying on a trade?
      `the company carries on a property business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company carrying on a property business?
      `the trade is my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your activities in the course of the trade your main employment?
      `I am paid through an intermediary for work that is my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you derive income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA (for example, through an intermediary)?
      `that income is from my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that income derived from activities that are your main employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as being in gainful self-employment through my company` IF
    `reg 77(3)(c) — the person is treated as being in gainful self-employment` `my company`
    WHERE
        `my company` MEANS `Person in relation to a company` WITH
            `the person stands in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company` IS `I stand in the position of a sole owner or partner of the company`
            `the company is carrying on a trade` IS `the company carries on a trade`
            `the company is carrying on a property business` IS `the company carries on a property business`
            `the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment` IS `the trade is my main employment`
            `the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA` IS `I am paid through an intermediary for work that is my main employment`
            `that income is derived from activities that are the person's main employment` IS `that income is from my main employment`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `value of the capital of the company` IS 0
            `fraction of the value that is the person's share` IS NOTHING
            `value of any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade` IS 0
            `the person is engaged in activities in the course of that trade` IS FALSE
            `the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having by virtue of paragraph (3)(b)` IS `the company's earnings placeholder`
            `employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee of the company` IS 0
        `the company's earnings placeholder` MEANS `Self-employed earnings considered under regulation 57` WITH
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `trades, professions or vocations carried on by the person in the assessment period` IS EMPTY
            `payments made by the person to HMRC in the assessment period by way of national insurance contributions or income tax in respect of any trade, profession or vocation` IS 0
            `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period` IS 0
            `a deduction has been made in respect of those contributions in calculating the person's employed earnings` IS FALSE
            `unused losses, oldest first` IS EMPTY

-- reg 77(3)(b), (4). The self-employed earnings of the company's trade are treated as the person's, in addition to the employed earnings the person
-- receives as a director or employee of the company. The seat asks about one trade of the company.
@export What earned income do I have from my company, in pounds (reg 77(3)(b), (4))?
GIVEN `I stand in the position of a sole owner or partner of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you stand in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company?
      `the company carries on a trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company carrying on a trade?
      `the company carries on a property business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company carrying on a property business?
      `I am paid through an intermediary for work that is my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you derive income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA (for example, through an intermediary)?
      `that income is from my main employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that income derived from activities that are your main employment?
      `what my business received in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did your trade, profession or vocation actually receive in the assessment period?
      `the value of what it received in kind` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value, in pounds, of any receipts in kind?
      `a tax refund relating to the business` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you receive as a refund or repayment of income tax, VAT or National Insurance contributions relating to the business? (0 if none)
      `the expenses I am allowed for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, are your allowed expenses for the assessment period (see the questions about regulations 58 and 59)?
      `the business is a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business carried on in a partnership?
      `my share of the partnership profit or loss` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what fraction of the profit or loss is yours? (for example 0.5 for a half; 0 if it is not a partnership)
      `what I paid HMRC for the business` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you pay HMRC in the assessment period by way of National Insurance contributions or income tax in respect of the business?
      `my relievable pension contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did you pay in relievable pension contributions in the assessment period?
      `those contributions were already deducted from my employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were those contributions already deducted when your employed earnings were worked out?
      `my unused losses from earlier periods` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your total of unused losses, in pounds, from earlier assessment periods and from the 12 months before your claim? (0 if none)
      `the employed earnings I receive as a director or employee of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What employed earnings, in pounds, do you receive as a director or employee of the company in the assessment period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What earned income do I have from my company` IS
    `reg 77(4) — the person's earned income from the company` `my company`
    WHERE
        `my company` MEANS `Person in relation to a company` WITH
            `the person stands in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company` IS `I stand in the position of a sole owner or partner of the company`
            `the company is carrying on a trade` IS `the company carries on a trade`
            `the company is carrying on a property business` IS `the company carries on a property business`
            `the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA` IS `I am paid through an intermediary for work that is my main employment`
            `that income is derived from activities that are the person's main employment` IS `that income is from my main employment`
            `the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having by virtue of paragraph (3)(b)` IS `my self-employed earnings`
            `employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee of the company` IS `the employed earnings I receive as a director or employee of the company`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `value of the capital of the company` IS 0
            `fraction of the value that is the person's share` IS NOTHING
            `value of any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade` IS 0
            `the person is engaged in activities in the course of that trade` IS FALSE
            `the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment` IS FALSE
        `my self-employed earnings` MEANS `Self-employed earnings considered under regulation 57` WITH
            `trades, professions or vocations carried on by the person in the assessment period` IS LIST `my business`
            `payments made by the person to HMRC in the assessment period by way of national insurance contributions or income tax in respect of any trade, profession or vocation` IS `what I paid HMRC for the business`
            `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period` IS `my relievable pension contributions`
            `a deduction has been made in respect of those contributions in calculating the person's employed earnings` IS `those contributions were already deducted from my employed earnings`
            `unused losses, oldest first` IS IF `my unused losses from earlier periods` GREATER THAN 0 THEN LIST `my unused losses from earlier periods` ELSE EMPTY
        `my business` MEANS `Trade, profession or vocation carried on in an assessment period` WITH
            `actual receipts in the assessment period` IS `what my business received in the period`
            `receipts in kind (their value)` IS `the value of what it received in kind`
            `any refund or repayment of income tax, value added tax or national insurance contributions relating to the trade, profession or vocation` IS `a tax refund relating to the business`
            `assets treated as receipts of the assessment period` IS EMPTY
            `amounts allowed as expenses under regulation 58 or 59` IS `the expenses I am allowed for the period`
            `share of the profit or loss attributable to the person, where the trade, profession or vocation is carried on in a partnership` IS IF `the business is a partnership` THEN JUST `my share of the partnership profit or loss` ELSE NOTHING


§§ `Part 7 -- The benefit cap (regulations 78 to 83)`

-- reg 78(2). For the benefit cap, a "couple" is joint claimants, or a single claimant who is a member of a couple and the other member.
@export Do I count as a couple for the benefit cap (reg 78(2))?
GIVEN `the basis of my claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Do you claim alone, jointly with your partner, or alone while being a member of a couple?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I count as a couple for the benefit cap` IF
    `reg 78(2) — the claim is by a couple` `the basis of my claim`

-- reg 79(1). Unless regulation 82 or 83 applies, the benefit cap applies where the welfare benefits you (or you and your partner) are entitled to
-- during the assessment period exceed the relevant amount.
@export Does the benefit cap apply to me (reg 79(1))?
GIVEN `all the welfare benefits I am entitled to in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total, in pounds, of the welfare benefits you (and your partner) are entitled to during the assessment period?
      `the cap for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the relevant amount, in pounds, that applies to you (see the question about regulation 80A)?
      `regulation 82 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 82 apply to you (your earnings are high enough, or you are in a grace period)?
      `regulation 83 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 83 apply to you (you or your child receive one of the listed benefits, or you have the carer or LCWRA element)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the benefit cap apply to me` IF
    `reg 79(1) — the benefit cap applies` `all the welfare benefits I am entitled to in the period` `the cap for the period` `regulation 82 applies to me` `regulation 83 applies to me`

-- reg 80. The amount of a welfare benefit used for the cap: universal credit before any reduction; nil for housing benefit; nil for an employment and
-- support allowance you are disqualified from; the amount taken into account as unearned income, if any; otherwise the amount awarded, as a monthly equivalent.
@export How much of this welfare benefit counts towards the benefit cap, in pounds a month (reg 80)?
GIVEN `what kind of benefit it is` IS A `Kind of welfare benefit for regulation 80` @desc What kind of welfare benefit is it?
      `what I am entitled to for the period it is awarded for` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, are you entitled to for the period for which the benefit is awarded, after any adjustment for overlapping benefits?
      `how often it is paid` IS A `Payment interval` @desc For what length of period is it awarded?
      `the universal credit before any reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is universal credit, how much, in pounds, are you entitled to before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act? (0 if it is not universal credit)
      `part of it counts as my unearned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an amount of it taken into account as your unearned income under regulation 66?
      `the amount counted as my unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in pounds? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of this welfare benefit counts towards the benefit cap` IS
    `reg 80 — the amount of a welfare benefit used` `my benefit`
    WHERE
        `my benefit` MEANS `Welfare benefit to which a person or couple is entitled during the reference period` WITH
            `kind` IS `what kind of benefit it is`
            `amount to which the person or couple is entitled for the period for which the benefit is awarded, after any adjustment in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992` IS `what I am entitled to for the period it is awarded for`
            `interval of the period for which the benefit is awarded` IS `how often it is paid`
            `amount of universal credit to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act` IS `the universal credit before any reduction`
            `amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66` IS IF `part of it counts as my unearned income` THEN JUST `the amount counted as my unearned income` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 80. The total of the welfare benefits you (and your partner) are entitled to during the assessment period, each used as regulation 80 says.
-- The seat asks for universal credit, housing benefit and up to three other welfare benefits.
@export What is the total of my welfare benefits for the benefit cap, in pounds a month (reg 80)?
GIVEN `my universal credit before any reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc How much universal credit, in pounds, are you entitled to before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act?
      `my housing benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much housing benefit, in pounds, are you entitled to? (It counts as nil towards the cap.)
      `the first other benefit I am entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, are you entitled to of your first other welfare benefit for the period it is awarded for, after any adjustment for overlapping benefits? (0 if none)
      `how often the first other benefit is paid` IS A `Payment interval` @desc For what length of period is your first other benefit awarded?
      `part of the first other benefit counts as my unearned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an amount of your first other benefit taken into account as your unearned income under regulation 66?
      `the amount of the first other benefit counted as my unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `the second other benefit I am entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, are you entitled to of your second other welfare benefit for the period it is awarded for, after any adjustment for overlapping benefits? (0 if none)
      `how often the second other benefit is paid` IS A `Payment interval` @desc For what length of period is your second other benefit awarded?
      `part of the second other benefit counts as my unearned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an amount of your second other benefit taken into account as your unearned income under regulation 66?
      `the amount of the second other benefit counted as my unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `the third other benefit I am entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, are you entitled to of your third other welfare benefit for the period it is awarded for, after any adjustment for overlapping benefits? (0 if none)
      `how often the third other benefit is paid` IS A `Payment interval` @desc For what length of period is your third other benefit awarded?
      `part of the third other benefit counts as my unearned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an amount of your third other benefit taken into account as your unearned income under regulation 66?
      `the amount of the third other benefit counted as my unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in pounds? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the total of my welfare benefits for the benefit cap` IS
    `reg 80 — the total entitlement to welfare benefits` (LIST `my universal credit item`, `my housing benefit item`, `my first other benefit`, `my second other benefit`, `my third other benefit`)
    WHERE
        `my universal credit item` MEANS `Welfare benefit to which a person or couple is entitled during the reference period` WITH
            `kind` IS `universal credit`
            `amount of universal credit to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act` IS `my universal credit before any reduction`
            -- Fields below are not read for this kind of benefit (universal credit reads only its own amount, housing benefit is nil, another benefit reads no universal credit amount).
            `amount to which the person or couple is entitled for the period for which the benefit is awarded, after any adjustment in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992` IS 0
            `interval of the period for which the benefit is awarded` IS `weekly payments`
            `amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66` IS NOTHING
        `my housing benefit item` MEANS `Welfare benefit to which a person or couple is entitled during the reference period` WITH
            `kind` IS `housing benefit under section 130 of the Contributions and Benefits Act`
            `amount to which the person or couple is entitled for the period for which the benefit is awarded, after any adjustment in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992` IS `my housing benefit`
            -- Fields below are not read for this kind of benefit (universal credit reads only its own amount, housing benefit is nil, another benefit reads no universal credit amount).
            `interval of the period for which the benefit is awarded` IS `weekly payments`
            `amount of universal credit to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act` IS 0
            `amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66` IS NOTHING
        `my first other benefit` MEANS `Welfare benefit to which a person or couple is entitled during the reference period` WITH
            `kind` IS `another welfare benefit`
            `amount to which the person or couple is entitled for the period for which the benefit is awarded, after any adjustment in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992` IS `the first other benefit I am entitled to`
            `interval of the period for which the benefit is awarded` IS `how often the first other benefit is paid`
            `amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66` IS IF `part of the first other benefit counts as my unearned income` THEN JUST `the amount of the first other benefit counted as my unearned income` ELSE NOTHING
            -- Fields below are not read for this kind of benefit (universal credit reads only its own amount, housing benefit is nil, another benefit reads no universal credit amount).
            `amount of universal credit to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act` IS 0
        `my second other benefit` MEANS `Welfare benefit to which a person or couple is entitled during the reference period` WITH
            `kind` IS `another welfare benefit`
            `amount to which the person or couple is entitled for the period for which the benefit is awarded, after any adjustment in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992` IS `the second other benefit I am entitled to`
            `interval of the period for which the benefit is awarded` IS `how often the second other benefit is paid`
            `amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66` IS IF `part of the second other benefit counts as my unearned income` THEN JUST `the amount of the second other benefit counted as my unearned income` ELSE NOTHING
            -- Fields below are not read for this kind of benefit (universal credit reads only its own amount, housing benefit is nil, another benefit reads no universal credit amount).
            `amount of universal credit to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act` IS 0
        `my third other benefit` MEANS `Welfare benefit to which a person or couple is entitled during the reference period` WITH
            `kind` IS `another welfare benefit`
            `amount to which the person or couple is entitled for the period for which the benefit is awarded, after any adjustment in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992` IS `the third other benefit I am entitled to`
            `interval of the period for which the benefit is awarded` IS `how often the third other benefit is paid`
            `amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66` IS IF `part of the third other benefit counts as my unearned income` THEN JUST `the amount of the third other benefit counted as my unearned income` ELSE NOTHING
            -- Fields below are not read for this kind of benefit (universal credit reads only its own amount, housing benefit is nil, another benefit reads no universal credit amount).
            `amount of universal credit to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act` IS 0

-- reg 80A(3). You are resident in Greater London if, where your award includes the housing costs element, the accommodation for which you meet the
-- occupation condition is there or you receive housing benefit for a dwelling there; otherwise, if the home you normally occupy is there or, if you have none, the
-- Jobcentre Plus office handling your claim is there.
@export Am I resident in Greater London for the benefit cap (reg 80A(3))?
GIVEN `my award includes the housing costs element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your award of universal credit include the housing costs element?
      `my accommodation for the occupation condition is in Greater London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is the accommodation in respect of which you meet the occupation condition in Greater London?
      `I get housing benefit for a dwelling in Greater London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in receipt of housing benefit in respect of a dwelling in Greater London?
      `I normally occupy accommodation as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there accommodation that you normally occupy as your home?
      `my home is in Greater London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accommodation that you normally occupy as your home in Greater London?
      `the Jobcentre Plus office handling my claim is in Greater London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Jobcentre Plus office to which the Secretary of State has allocated your claim in Greater London?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I resident in Greater London for the benefit cap` IF
    `reg 80A(3) — the claimant is resident in Greater London` `my accommodation`
    WHERE
        `my accommodation` MEANS `Accommodation of a claimant for regulation 80A(3)` WITH
            `the housing costs element is included in the claimant's award of universal credit` IS `my award includes the housing costs element`
            `accommodation in respect of which the claimant meets the occupation condition is in Greater London` IS `my accommodation for the occupation condition is in Greater London`
            `the claimant is in receipt of housing benefit in respect of a dwelling in Greater London` IS `I get housing benefit for a dwelling in Greater London`
            `there is accommodation that the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS `I normally occupy accommodation as my home`
            `accommodation that the claimant normally occupies as their home is in Greater London` IS `my home is in Greater London`
            `the Jobcentre Plus office to which the Secretary of State has allocated the claim is in Greater London` IS `the Jobcentre Plus office handling my claim is in Greater London`

-- reg 80A(2). The applicable annual limit: 16,967 pounds for a single claimant resident in Greater London not responsible for a child or qualifying young person;
-- 25,323 pounds for joint claimants either of whom is resident there, or a single claimant resident there who is responsible for a child or qualifying young person;
-- 14,753 pounds for a single claimant not resident there and not so responsible; 22,020 pounds for joint claimants not resident there and for a single claimant
-- not resident there who is so responsible. A single claimant who is a member of a couple is taken as a single claimant (fork F-C2 in NOTES.md).
@export What is the annual limit of the benefit cap for me, in pounds (reg 80A(2))?
GIVEN `the basis of my claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Do you claim alone, jointly with your partner, or alone while being a member of a couple?
      `I am resident in Greater London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Greater London (see the question about regulation 80A(3))?
      `my joint claimant is resident in Greater London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, is the other joint claimant resident in Greater London? (No, if you claim alone)
      `I am responsible for a child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you responsible for a child or qualifying young person?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the annual limit of the benefit cap for me` IS
    `reg 80A(2) — the applicable annual limit` `the basis of my claim` `I am resident in Greater London` `my joint claimant is resident in Greater London` `I am responsible for a child or qualifying young person`

-- reg 80A(1). The relevant amount is the applicable annual limit divided by 12.
@export What is the monthly level of the benefit cap for me, in pounds (reg 80A(1))?
GIVEN `the basis of my claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Do you claim alone, jointly with your partner, or alone while being a member of a couple?
      `I am resident in Greater London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Greater London (see the question about regulation 80A(3))?
      `my joint claimant is resident in Greater London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, is the other joint claimant resident in Greater London? (No, if you claim alone)
      `I am responsible for a child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you responsible for a child or qualifying young person?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the monthly level of the benefit cap for me` IS
    `reg 80A(1) — the relevant amount` (`reg 80A(2) — the applicable annual limit` `the basis of my claim` `I am resident in Greater London` `my joint claimant is resident in Greater London` `I am responsible for a child or qualifying young person`)

-- reg 81(3). The excess is the total of the welfare benefits you (and your partner) are entitled to in the reference period, minus the relevant amount.
@export By how much do my welfare benefits exceed the benefit cap, in pounds (reg 81(3))?
GIVEN `all the welfare benefits I am entitled to in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total, in pounds, of the welfare benefits you (and your partner) are entitled to in the reference period?
      `the cap for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the relevant amount, in pounds, that applies to you?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much do my welfare benefits exceed the benefit cap` IS
    `reg 81(3) — the excess` `all the welfare benefits I am entitled to in the period` `the cap for the period`

-- reg 81(1), (2). Where the cap applies, your award for the assessment period is reduced by the excess minus any amount included in the award for the childcare
-- costs element; and not at all where the childcare costs element is greater than the excess.
@export By how much is my universal credit reduced by the benefit cap, in pounds (reg 81(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the benefit cap applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the benefit cap apply to you in this assessment period?
      `the excess` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the excess, in pounds (see the question about regulation 81(3))?
      `my childcare costs element` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, is included in your award for the childcare costs element for the assessment period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much is my universal credit reduced by the benefit cap` IS
    `reg 81(1) and (2) — the reduction of the award` `the benefit cap applies to me` `the excess` `my childcare costs element`

-- reg 81(1). The amount of your award after the reduction. The text does not say what happens if the reduction is more than the award,
-- so there the answer is "nothing" (not covered).
@export What is my universal credit award after the benefit cap reduction, in pounds (reg 81(1))?
GIVEN `my award before the reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, is your award for the assessment period before the reduction?
      `the reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the reduction, in pounds (see the question about regulation 81(1) and (2))?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my universal credit award after the benefit cap reduction` IS
    `reg 81(1) — the amount of the award after the reduction` `my award before the reduction` `the reduction`

-- reg 82(1)(a). The earnings threshold: what a person would be paid at the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours
-- a week, converted to a month by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12, any fraction of a pound disregarded.
@export What is the earnings threshold that exempts me from the benefit cap, in pounds a month (reg 82(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the National Minimum Wage hourly rate at the start of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the earnings threshold that exempts me from the benefit cap` IS
    `reg 82(1)(a) — the earnings threshold` `the National Minimum Wage hourly rate at the start of the period`

-- reg 82(1)(a), (4). If your earned income (or your and your partner's combined) equals or exceeds the earnings threshold, the benefit cap does not
-- apply; earned income here does not include income you are treated as having under the minimum income floor (reg 62).
@export Do I earn enough to be exempt from the benefit cap (reg 82(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my earned income, or ours combined, for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, for the assessment period, not counting income you are treated as having under the minimum income floor?
      `the National Minimum Wage hourly rate at the start of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month, in pounds?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I earn enough to be exempt from the benefit cap` IF
    `reg 82(1)(a) — the earned income equals or exceeds the earnings threshold` `my earned income, or ours combined, for the period` `the National Minimum Wage hourly rate at the start of the period`

-- reg 82(3). The condition for a grace period: in each of the 12 months immediately before the day, your earned income (or your and your partner's
-- combined) equalled or exceeded the earnings threshold of reg 82(1)(a), with the rate in force at the start of that month.
@export Did I earn enough in each of the last 12 months for a grace period (reg 82(3))?
GIVEN `my earned income in the first month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the month immediately before that day, not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the first month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the second month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the second month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the second month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the third month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the third month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the third month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the fourth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the fourth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the fourth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the fifth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the fifth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the fifth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the sixth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the sixth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the sixth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the seventh month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the seventh month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the seventh month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the eighth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the eighth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the eighth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the ninth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the ninth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the ninth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the tenth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the tenth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the tenth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the eleventh month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the eleventh month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the eleventh month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the twelfth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the twelfth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the twelfth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I earn enough in each of the last 12 months for a grace period` IF
    `reg 82(3) — the condition is met` (LIST `the first month`, `the second month`, `the third month`, `the fourth month`, `the fifth month`, `the sixth month`, `the seventh month`, `the eighth month`, `the ninth month`, `the tenth month`, `the eleventh month`, `the twelfth month`)
    WHERE
        `the first month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the first month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the first month`
        `the second month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the second month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the second month`
        `the third month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the third month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the third month`
        `the fourth month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the fourth month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the fourth month`
        `the fifth month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the fifth month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the fifth month`
        `the sixth month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the sixth month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the sixth month`
        `the seventh month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the seventh month`
