-- reg 82(1)(b). The benefit cap does not apply in an assessment period that falls within a grace period or is one in which a grace period begins or ends.
@export Does my assessment period fall in a grace period from the benefit cap (reg 82(1)(b))?
GIVEN `first day of my grace period` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your grace period begin?
      `last day of my grace period` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your grace period end?
      `first day of the assessment period I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the assessment period you are asking about begin?
      `last day of the assessment period I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date does it end?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my assessment period fall in a grace period from the benefit cap` IF
    `reg 82(1)(b) — the assessment period is within a grace period or one in which it begins or ends` `my grace period` `the assessment period I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `my grace period` MEANS `Grace period` WITH
            `first day of the grace period` IS `first day of my grace period`
            `last day of the grace period` IS `last day of my grace period`
        `the assessment period I am asking about` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `first day of the assessment period I am asking about`
            `last day` IS `last day of the assessment period I am asking about`

-- reg 82(1). The benefit cap does not apply in an assessment period where your earned income (or your and your partner's combined) equals or exceeds the
-- earnings threshold, or where the period falls within a grace period or is one in which a grace period begins or ends. The seat takes one candidate
-- day on which a grace period may begin, as in the question on the end of a grace period.
@export Am I exempt from the benefit cap because of my earnings (reg 82(1))?
GIVEN `my earned income, or ours combined, for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, for the assessment period, not counting income you are treated as having under the minimum income floor?
      `the National Minimum Wage hourly rate at the start of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month, in pounds?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what date would the grace period begin?
      `the day is in my current period of entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the day fall within your current period of entitlement to universal credit?
      `the day is the first day of an assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day the first day of an assessment period?
      `my earned income in the assessment period beginning that day` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your earned income (or your and your partner's combined), in pounds, in that assessment period, not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of that assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that assessment period?
      `the day is before my current period of entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the day fall before your current period of entitlement to universal credit?
      `I stopped paid work on the day before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease paid work on the day before?
      `my earned income in the first month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the month immediately before that day, not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the first month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the second month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the second month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the second month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the third month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the third month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the third month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the fourth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the fourth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the fourth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the fifth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the fifth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the fifth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the sixth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the sixth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the sixth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the seventh month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the seventh month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the seventh month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the eighth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the eighth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the eighth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the ninth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the ninth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the ninth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the tenth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the tenth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the tenth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the eleventh month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the eleventh month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the eleventh month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `my earned income in the twelfth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earned income (or your and your partner's combined earned income), in pounds, in the twelfth month before that day (counting back from the month immediately before it), not counting income treated as had under the minimum income floor?
      `the hourly rate at the start of the twelfth month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds, in force at the beginning of that month?
      `first day of the assessment period I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the assessment period you are asking about begin?
      `last day of the assessment period I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date does it end?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I exempt from the benefit cap because of my earnings` IF
    `reg 82(1) — the benefit cap does not apply by reason of earnings` `my earned income, or ours combined, for the period` `the National Minimum Wage hourly rate at the start of the period` (LIST `the candidate day`) `the assessment period I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `the candidate day` MEANS `Day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `day` IS `the day`
            `the day falls within the current period of entitlement to universal credit` IS `the day is in my current period of entitlement`
            `the day is the first day of an assessment period` IS `the day is the first day of an assessment period`
            `earned income in that assessment period, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the assessment period beginning that day`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of that assessment period` IS `the hourly rate at the start of that assessment period`
            `the day falls before the current period of entitlement to universal credit` IS `the day is before my current period of entitlement`
            `the claimant ceased paid work on the day before` IS `I stopped paid work on the day before`
            `the 12 months immediately preceding that day` IS LIST `the first month`, `the second month`, `the third month`, `the fourth month`, `the fifth month`, `the sixth month`, `the seventh month`, `the eighth month`, `the ninth month`, `the tenth month`, `the eleventh month`, `the twelfth month`
        `the first month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the first month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the first month`
        `the second month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the second month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the second month`
        `the third month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the third month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the third month`
        `the fourth month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the fourth month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the fourth month`
        `the fifth month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the fifth month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the fifth month`
        `the sixth month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the sixth month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the sixth month`
        `the seventh month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the seventh month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the seventh month`
        `the eighth month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the eighth month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the eighth month`
        `the ninth month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the ninth month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the ninth month`
        `the tenth month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the tenth month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the tenth month`
        `the eleventh month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the eleventh month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the eleventh month`
        `the twelfth month` MEANS `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` WITH
            `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS `my earned income in the twelfth month`
            `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month` IS `the hourly rate at the start of the twelfth month`
        `the assessment period I am asking about` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `first day of the assessment period I am asking about`
            `last day` IS `last day of the assessment period I am asking about`

-- reg 83(2). A "war pension" is a pension or allowance under a listed instrument to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner or in respect of
-- disablement; a Crown pension otherwise than under an enactment; a payment under one of three old orders to the widow, widower or surviving civil partner of
-- someone whose service ended before 31 March 1973; or an analogous foreign pension.
@export Is my pension a war pension (reg 83(2))?
GIVEN `it is a pension or allowance under an instrument listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a pension or allowance payable under any of the instruments listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA?
      `it is paid to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner?
      `it is paid in respect of disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable in respect of disablement?
      `it is a Crown pension for people disabled or killed in armed forces service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a pension payable to a person as a widow, widower or surviving civil partner under a power of the Crown to make provision about pensions for or in respect of persons who have been disabled or have died in consequence of service as members of the armed forces of the Crown?
      `the provision is an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the Senedd` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision under which it is paid an enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales?
      `the provision is an instrument under such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales?
      `the provision is an enactment in some other way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision an enactment apart from those?
      `it is paid under one of the three old orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment made under the Order in Council of 19th December 1881, the Royal Warrant of 27th October 1884 or the Order by His Majesty of 14th January 1922?
      `it is paid to the widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person who died of service in an analogous capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person whose death was attributable to service in a capacity analogous to service as a member of the armed forces of the Crown?
      `that service has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person's service in such a capacity ended?
      `the day that service ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (any date if not)
      `it is paid by a government outside the United Kingdom and is like those pensions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a pension paid by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom which is analogous to those pensions, allowances or payments?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my pension a war pension` IF
    `reg 83(2) — war pension` `my pension`
    WHERE
        `my pension` MEANS `Pension that may be a war pension` WITH
            `pension or allowance payable under an instrument listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA` IS `it is a pension or allowance under an instrument listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA`
            `payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner` IS `it is paid to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner`
            `payable in respect of disablement` IS `it is paid in respect of disablement`
            `pension payable to a person as a widow, widower or surviving civil partner under a power of the Crown to make provision about pensions for or in respect of persons who have been disabled or have died in consequence of service as members of the armed forces of the Crown` IS `it is a Crown pension for people disabled or killed in armed forces service`
            `provision under which the pension is paid` IS `the provision it is paid under`
            `payment made under the Order in Council of 19th December 1881, the Royal Warrant of 27th October 1884 or the Order by His Majesty of 14th January 1922` IS `it is paid under one of the three old orders`
            `payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person whose death was attributable to service in a capacity analogous to service as a member of the armed forces of the Crown` IS `it is paid to the widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person who died of service in an analogous capacity`
            `date on which that person's service in such a capacity terminated` IS IF `that service has ended` THEN JUST `the day that service ended` ELSE NOTHING
            `pension paid by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom which is analogous to a pension, allowance or payment mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (c)` IS `it is paid by a government outside the United Kingdom and is like those pensions`
        `the provision it is paid under` MEANS `Provision whose standing as an enactment is asked by uc2` WITH
            `enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales` IS `the provision is an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the Senedd`
            `instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales` IS `the provision is an instrument under such an Act`
            `an enactment apart from the inclusions in regulation 2` IS `the provision is an enactment in some other way`

-- reg 83(1)(a), (j). The benefit cap does not apply where the LCWRA element is included in the award, or a claimant is receiving an employment
-- and support allowance that includes the support component, or the carer element is included in the award.
@export Am I exempt from the benefit cap because of my LCWRA, support component or carer element (reg 83(1)(a), (j))?
GIVEN `my award includes the LCWRA element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the LCWRA element included in your award of universal credit?
      `I receive an employment and support allowance with the support component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a claimant receiving an employment and support allowance that includes the support component?
      `my award includes the carer element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the carer element included in your award of universal credit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I exempt from the benefit cap because of my LCWRA, support component or carer element` IF
    `reg 83(1) — the benefit cap does not apply by reason of the benefits received` `my household`
    WHERE
        `my household` MEANS `Household for regulation 83` WITH
            `members` IS EMPTY
            `the LCWRA element is included in the award of universal credit` IS `my award includes the LCWRA element`
            `a claimant is receiving an employment and support allowance that includes the support component` IS `I receive an employment and support allowance with the support component`
            `the carer element is included in the award of universal credit` IS `my award includes the carer element`

-- reg 83(1)(b) to (i), (k). The benefit cap does not apply where a claimant (or, for some of the payments, a child or qualifying young person)
-- is receiving, or in the listed cases is entitled to, one of the listed payments. Ask once for each payment; any one is enough. A war pension counts only
-- if it is a war pension within paragraph (2), so the facts about the pension are asked as well (answer "no" if it is not a war pension).
@export Am I exempt from the benefit cap because of a disability, injury or carer payment (reg 83(1)(b) to (k))?
GIVEN `which payment it is` IS A `Payment named in regulation 83` @desc Which of these payments is it?
      `who it is for` IS A `Person in the household` @desc Who receives it, or is entitled to it?
      `whether they receive it` IS A `Position of a person as to a payment` @desc Are they receiving it, or are they entitled to it but not receiving it, and if so why?
      `it is a pension or allowance under an instrument listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a pension or allowance payable under any of the instruments listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA?
      `it is paid to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner?
      `it is paid in respect of disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable in respect of disablement?
      `it is a Crown pension for people disabled or killed in armed forces service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a pension payable to a person as a widow, widower or surviving civil partner under a power of the Crown to make provision about pensions for or in respect of persons who have been disabled or have died in consequence of service as members of the armed forces of the Crown?
      `the provision is an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the Senedd` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision under which it is paid an enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales?
      `the provision is an instrument under such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales?
      `the provision is an enactment in some other way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision an enactment apart from those?
      `it is paid under one of the three old orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment made under the Order in Council of 19th December 1881, the Royal Warrant of 27th October 1884 or the Order by His Majesty of 14th January 1922?
      `it is paid to the widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person who died of service in an analogous capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person whose death was attributable to service in a capacity analogous to service as a member of the armed forces of the Crown?
      `that service has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person's service in such a capacity ended?
      `the day that service ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (any date if not)
      `it is paid by a government outside the United Kingdom and is like those pensions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a pension paid by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom which is analogous to those pensions, allowances or payments?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I exempt from the benefit cap because of a disability, injury or carer payment` IF
    `reg 83(1) — the benefit cap does not apply by reason of the benefits received` `my household`
    WHERE
        `my household` MEANS `Household for regulation 83` WITH
            `members` IS LIST `the person who gets the payment`
            -- The other ways of being exempt (the LCWRA element, the support component, the carer element) are answered by the previous question; FALSE here means not asked, not does not apply.
            `the LCWRA element is included in the award of universal credit` IS FALSE
            `a claimant is receiving an employment and support allowance that includes the support component` IS FALSE
            `the carer element is included in the award of universal credit` IS FALSE
        `the person who gets the payment` MEANS `Member of the household for regulation 83` WITH
            `role` IS `who it is for`
            `payments` IS LIST `the payment`
        `the payment` MEANS `Payment to a person for regulation 83` WITH
            `payment` IS `which payment it is`
            `position` IS `whether they receive it`
            `pension` IS `my pension`
        `my pension` MEANS `Pension that may be a war pension` WITH
            `pension or allowance payable under an instrument listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA` IS `it is a pension or allowance under an instrument listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA`
            `payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner` IS `it is paid to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner`
            `payable in respect of disablement` IS `it is paid in respect of disablement`
            `pension payable to a person as a widow, widower or surviving civil partner under a power of the Crown to make provision about pensions for or in respect of persons who have been disabled or have died in consequence of service as members of the armed forces of the Crown` IS `it is a Crown pension for people disabled or killed in armed forces service`
            `provision under which the pension is paid` IS `the provision it is paid under`
            `payment made under the Order in Council of 19th December 1881, the Royal Warrant of 27th October 1884 or the Order by His Majesty of 14th January 1922` IS `it is paid under one of the three old orders`
            `payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person whose death was attributable to service in a capacity analogous to service as a member of the armed forces of the Crown` IS `it is paid to the widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person who died of service in an analogous capacity`
            `date on which that person's service in such a capacity terminated` IS IF `that service has ended` THEN JUST `the day that service ended` ELSE NOTHING
            `pension paid by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom which is analogous to a pension, allowance or payment mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (c)` IS `it is paid by a government outside the United Kingdom and is like those pensions`
        `the provision it is paid under` MEANS `Provision whose standing as an enactment is asked by uc2` WITH
            `enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales` IS `the provision is an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the Senedd`
            `instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales` IS `the provision is an instrument under such an Act`
            `an enactment apart from the inclusions in regulation 2` IS `the provision is an enactment in some other way`


§ `Schedule 10 -- Capital to be disregarded (regulation 48(1))`

-- Regulation 48(1) disregards the capital that Schedule 10 specifies. Each question below asks whether capital of one paragraph's kind is
-- disregarded; "yes" is the answer to regulation 48(1) for that capital. The "past 6 months" of the paragraphs is the period of reg 48(2).

§§ `Premises`

-- Sch 10 para 1(1). Premises you occupy as your home are disregarded; only one set of premises may be treated as your home (para 1(2)).
@export Are the premises I live in as my home disregarded (Sch 10 para 1(1))?
GIVEN `I occupy the premises as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you occupy the premises as your home?
      `they are the one set of premises I treat as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they the one set of premises treated as your home?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the premises I live in as my home disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 1(1) — premises occupied as the person's home` `I occupy the premises as my home` `they are the one set of premises I treat as my home`

-- Sch 10 para 1(2). For paragraphs 1 to 5, only one set of premises may be treated as your home. The seat takes up to three sets.
@export Is only one set of premises treated as my home (Sch 10 para 1(2))?
GIVEN `I treat my first set of premises as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you treat your first set of premises as your home?
      `I treat my second set of premises as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you treat your second set of premises (if any) as your home?
      `I treat my third set of premises as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you treat your third set of premises (if any) as your home?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is only one set of premises treated as my home` IF
    `Sch 10 para 1(2) — at most one set of premises is treated as the person's home` (LIST `I treat my first set of premises as my home`, `I treat my second set of premises as my home`, `I treat my third set of premises as my home`)

-- Sch 10 para 2. Premises occupied by a close relative of yours as their home are disregarded where the relative has limited capability for work or
-- has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit.
@export Are the premises my close relative lives in disregarded (Sch 10 para 2)?
GIVEN `my relative occupies the premises as their home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a close relative of yours occupy the premises as their home?
      `how they are related to me` IS A `Listed relation` @desc How is the relative related to you?
      `how their partner is related to me` IS A `Listed relation` @desc If the relative has a partner who also lives there, how is that partner related to you? (not a listed relation, if none)
      `my relative has limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the relative have limited capability for work?
      `my relative has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the relative reached the qualifying age for state pension credit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the premises my close relative lives in disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 2 — premises occupied by a close relative` `my relative occupies the premises as their home` `my relative` `my relative's capability for work` `my relative has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`
    WHERE
        `my relative` MEANS `Possible close relative` WITH
            `relation to the person` IS `how they are related to me`
            `relation of the partner to the person` IS `how their partner is related to me`
        `my relative's capability for work` MEANS `Capability for work` WITH
            `limited capability for work` IS `my relative has limited capability for work`
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS FALSE
            `severe conditions criteria claimant` IS FALSE

-- Sch 10 para 3. Premises occupied by your former partner as their home are disregarded where you are not estranged but living apart by force of
-- circumstances, for example where you are in residential care.
@export Are the premises my former partner lives in disregarded (Sch 10 para 3)?
GIVEN `my former partner occupies the premises as their home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your former partner occupy the premises as their home?
      `we are not estranged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and your former partner not estranged?
      `we live apart by force of circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you living apart by force of circumstances (for example, because you are in residential care)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the premises my former partner lives in disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 3 — premises occupied by a former partner` `my former partner occupies the premises as their home` `we are not estranged` `we live apart by force of circumstances`

-- Sch 10 para 4(1). Premises you intend to occupy as your home are disregarded where, within the past 6 months, you acquired them but have not yet
-- moved in, or began taking steps to obtain possession, or began essential repairs or alterations to make them fit for occupation.
@export Are the premises I intend to live in disregarded (Sch 10 para 4(1))?
GIVEN `I intend to occupy the premises as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to occupy the premises as your home?
      `they are the one set of premises I treat as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they the one set of premises treated as your home?
      `I acquired the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you acquired the premises?
      `the day I acquired them` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (any date if not)
      `I have not yet moved in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not yet taken up occupation?
      `I am taking steps to obtain possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking steps to obtain possession?
      `I first sought legal advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you sought legal advice about it?
      `the day I first sought legal advice` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date was it first sought? (any date if not)
      `proceedings have been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have proceedings been commenced?
      `the day proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (any date if not)
      `I am carrying out essential repairs or alterations to make it fit to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you carrying out essential repairs or alterations required to render the premises fit for occupation?
      `the day the repairs or alterations began` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date were they commenced? (any date if not)
      `I have started the repairs or alterations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they been commenced?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
      `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State extended the 6-month period in your case?
      `the months it has been extended to` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, to how many months? (0 if not extended)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the premises I intend to live in disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 4(1) — premises the person intends to occupy as their home` `my premises` `the day my capital is being worked out` (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (IF `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` THEN JUST `the months it has been extended to` ELSE NOTHING))
    WHERE
        `my premises` MEANS `Premises that a person intends to occupy as their home` WITH
            `the person intends to occupy the premises as their home` IS `I intend to occupy the premises as my home`
            `the premises are the one set treated as the person's home` IS `they are the one set of premises I treat as my home`
            `date on which the person acquired the premises` IS IF `I acquired the premises` THEN JUST `the day I acquired them` ELSE NOTHING
            `the person has not yet taken up occupation` IS `I have not yet moved in`
            `the person is taking steps to obtain possession` IS `I am taking steps to obtain possession`
            `date on which legal advice was first sought` IS IF `I first sought legal advice` THEN JUST `the day I first sought legal advice` ELSE NOTHING
            `date on which proceedings were commenced` IS IF `proceedings have been commenced` THEN JUST `the day proceedings were commenced` ELSE NOTHING
            `the person is carrying out essential repairs or alterations required to render the premises fit for occupation` IS `I am carrying out essential repairs or alterations to make it fit to live in`
            `date on which the repairs or alterations were commenced` IS IF `I have started the repairs or alterations` THEN JUST `the day the repairs or alterations began` ELSE NOTHING

-- Sch 10 para 4(2). You are taken to have commenced steps to obtain possession of premises on the date that legal advice is first sought or
-- proceedings are commenced, whichever is earlier.
@export On what date am I taken to have begun steps to obtain possession (Sch 10 para 4(2))?
GIVEN `I am taking steps to obtain possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking steps to obtain possession?
      `I first sought legal advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you sought legal advice about it?
      `the day I first sought legal advice` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date was it first sought? (any date if not)
      `proceedings have been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have proceedings been commenced?
      `the day proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (any date if not)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what date am I taken to have begun steps to obtain possession` IS
    `Sch 10 para 4(2) — the date steps to obtain possession are taken to have commenced` `my premises`
    WHERE
        `my premises` MEANS `Premises that a person intends to occupy as their home` WITH
            `the person is taking steps to obtain possession` IS `I am taking steps to obtain possession`
            `date on which legal advice was first sought` IS IF `I first sought legal advice` THEN JUST `the day I first sought legal advice` ELSE NOTHING
            `date on which proceedings were commenced` IS IF `proceedings have been commenced` THEN JUST `the day proceedings were commenced` ELSE NOTHING
            -- Placeholders below: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the person intends to occupy the premises as their home` IS FALSE
            `the premises are the one set treated as the person's home` IS FALSE
            `date on which the person acquired the premises` IS NOTHING
            `the person has not yet taken up occupation` IS FALSE
            `the person is carrying out essential repairs or alterations required to render the premises fit for occupation` IS FALSE
            `date on which the repairs or alterations were commenced` IS NOTHING

-- Sch 10 para 5. Premises you have ceased to occupy as your home following an estrangement from your former partner are disregarded where you ceased to
-- occupy them within the past 6 months, or your former partner is a lone parent and occupies them as their home.
@export Are the premises I left after an estrangement disregarded (Sch 10 para 5)?
GIVEN `I left the premises after an estrangement from my former partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to occupy the premises as your home following an estrangement from your former partner?
      `they are the one set of premises I treat as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they the one set of premises treated as your home?
      `the day I left them` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you cease to occupy the premises?
      `my former partner is a lone parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your former partner a lone parent?
      `my former partner lives there as their home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your former partner occupy the premises as their home?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
      `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State extended the 6-month period in your case?
      `the months it has been extended to` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, to how many months? (0 if not extended)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the premises I left after an estrangement disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 5 — premises ceased to be occupied after an estrangement` `my premises` `the day my capital is being worked out` (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (IF `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` THEN JUST `the months it has been extended to` ELSE NOTHING))
    WHERE
        `my premises` MEANS `Premises that a person has ceased to occupy after an estrangement` WITH
            `the person has ceased to occupy the premises as their home following an estrangement from their former partner` IS `I left the premises after an estrangement from my former partner`
            `the premises are the one set treated as the person's home` IS `they are the one set of premises I treat as my home`
            `date on which the person ceased to occupy the premises` IS `the day I left them`
            `the former partner is a lone parent` IS `my former partner is a lone parent`
            `the former partner occupies the premises as their home` IS `my former partner lives there as their home`

-- Sch 10 para 6. Premises you are taking reasonable steps to dispose of are disregarded where those steps were commenced within the past 6 months.
@export Are the premises I am trying to sell disregarded (Sch 10 para 6)?
GIVEN `I am taking reasonable steps to dispose of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking reasonable steps to dispose of the premises?
      `the day I began those steps` IS A DATE @desc On what date were those steps commenced?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
      `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State extended the 6-month period in your case?
      `the months it has been extended to` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, to how many months? (0 if not extended)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the premises I am trying to sell disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 6 — premises the person is taking reasonable steps to dispose of` `I am taking reasonable steps to dispose of the premises` `the day I began those steps` `the day my capital is being worked out` (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (IF `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` THEN JUST `the months it has been extended to` ELSE NOTHING))


§§ `Business assets`

-- Sch 10 para 7. Assets used wholly or mainly for a trade, profession or vocation which you are carrying on are disregarded.
@export Are the assets I use for my business disregarded (Sch 10 para 7)?
GIVEN `I use the assets wholly or mainly for a trade, profession or vocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the assets used wholly or mainly for the purposes of a trade, profession or vocation?
      `I am carrying on that trade, profession or vocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you carrying on that trade, profession or vocation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the assets I use for my business disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 7 — assets used for a trade, profession or vocation the person carries on` `I use the assets wholly or mainly for a trade, profession or vocation` `I am carrying on that trade, profession or vocation`

-- Sch 10 para 8. Assets used for a business you stopped within the past 6 months are disregarded if you are taking reasonable steps to dispose of
-- them, or you stopped because of incapacity and can reasonably expect to be reengaged on recovery.
@export Are the assets of a business I have stopped disregarded (Sch 10 para 8)?
GIVEN `the assets were used for a business that I have ceased to carry on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the assets used wholly or mainly for a trade, profession or vocation that you have ceased to carry on?
      `the day I stopped` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you cease to carry it on?
      `I am taking reasonable steps to dispose of the assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking reasonable steps to dispose of the assets?
      `I stopped because of incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be engaged in carrying it on because of incapacity?
      `I can reasonably expect to be reengaged on recovery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you reasonably expect to be reengaged on recovery?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
      `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State extended the 6-month period in your case?
      `the months it has been extended to` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, to how many months? (0 if not extended)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the assets of a business I have stopped disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 8 — assets of a trade, profession or vocation ceased within the past period` `my business assets` `the day my capital is being worked out` (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (IF `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` THEN JUST `the months it has been extended to` ELSE NOTHING))
    WHERE
        `my business assets` MEANS `Assets of a trade, profession or vocation that has ceased` WITH
            `assets were used wholly or mainly for a trade, profession or vocation that the person has ceased to carry on` IS `the assets were used for a business that I have ceased to carry on`
            `date on which the person ceased to carry it on` IS `the day I stopped`
            `the person is taking reasonable steps to dispose of the assets` IS `I am taking reasonable steps to dispose of the assets`
            `the person ceased to be engaged in carrying it on because of incapacity` IS `I stopped because of incapacity`
            `the person can reasonably expect to be reengaged on recovery` IS `I can reasonably expect to be reengaged on recovery`


§§ `Rights in pension schemes etc`

-- Sch 10 para 9. The value of any policy of life insurance is disregarded.
@export Is the value of my life insurance policy disregarded (Sch 10 para 9)?
GIVEN `the capital is the value of a policy of life insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the capital the value of a policy of life insurance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the value of my life insurance policy disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 9 — the value of a policy of life insurance` `the capital is the value of a policy of life insurance`

-- Sch 10 para 10. The value of any right to receive a pension under an occupational or personal pension scheme, or another scheme registered under
-- section 153 of the Finance Act 2004, is disregarded.
@export Is the value of my right to a pension disregarded (Sch 10 para 10)?
GIVEN `the capital is the value of a right to receive a pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the capital the value of a right to receive a pension?
      `it is under an occupational pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it under an occupational pension scheme within the meaning of section 1 of the Pension Schemes Act 1993?
      `it is under a personal pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it under a personal pension scheme within the meaning of section 1 of the Pension Schemes Act 1993?
      `it is under another pension scheme registered under section 153 of the Finance Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it under another pension scheme registered under section 153 of the Finance Act 2004?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the value of my right to a pension disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 10 — the value of a right to receive a pension` `my pension right`
    WHERE
        `my pension right` MEANS `Right to receive a pension` WITH
            `the capital is the value of a right to receive a pension` IS `the capital is the value of a right to receive a pension`
            `occupational pension scheme within the meaning of section 1 of the Pension Schemes Act 1993` IS `it is under an occupational pension scheme`
            `personal pension scheme within the meaning of section 1 of the Pension Schemes Act 1993` IS `it is under a personal pension scheme`
            `other pension scheme registered under section 153 of the Finance Act 2004` IS `it is under another pension scheme registered under section 153 of the Finance Act 2004`

-- Sch 10 para 11. The value of a funeral plan contract is disregarded: a contract under which you make payments to secure the provision of a funeral,
-- where the sole purpose of the plan is the provision of a funeral.
@export Is the value of my funeral plan disregarded (Sch 10 para 11)?
GIVEN `the capital is the value of a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the capital the value of a contract?
      `I make payments under it to secure a funeral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a contract under which you make payments to a person to secure the provision of a funeral?
      `the sole purpose of the plan is a funeral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sole purpose of the plan the provision of a funeral?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the value of my funeral plan disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 11(1) — the value of a funeral plan contract` `the capital is the value of a contract` `I make payments under it to secure a funeral` `the sole purpose of the plan is a funeral`


§§ `Amounts earmarked for special purposes`

-- Sch 10 para 12. An amount deposited with a housing association as a condition of your occupying premises as your home is disregarded.
@export Is a deposit I paid to a housing association disregarded (Sch 10 para 12)?
GIVEN `the amount is deposited with a housing association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount deposited with a housing association?
      `the deposit is a condition of my living in the premises as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the deposit a condition of your occupying premises as your home?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a deposit I paid to a housing association disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 12 — an amount deposited with a housing association` `the amount is deposited with a housing association` `the deposit is a condition of my living in the premises as my home`

-- Sch 10 para 13. An amount received within the past 6 months to be used to buy premises you intend to occupy as your home is disregarded where it
-- is from the sale of your former home, or deposited with a housing association as in paragraph 12, or a grant made for the sole purpose of buying a home.
@export Is an amount I received to buy a home disregarded (Sch 10 para 13)?
GIVEN `the amount is to be used to buy premises I intend to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount to be used for the purchase of premises that you intend to occupy as your home?
      `the day I received the amount` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the amount?
      `it comes from selling my former home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it attributable to the proceeds of the sale of premises formerly occupied by you as your home?
      `it has been deposited with a housing association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been deposited with a housing association as mentioned in paragraph 12?
      `it is a grant made only to buy a home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a grant made to you for the sole purpose of the purchase of a home?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
      `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State extended the 6-month period in your case?
      `the months it has been extended to` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, to how many months? (0 if not extended)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an amount I received to buy a home disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 13 — an amount received for the purchase of a home` `my amount` `the day my capital is being worked out` (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (IF `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` THEN JUST `the months it has been extended to` ELSE NOTHING))
    WHERE
        `my amount` MEANS `Amount received for the purchase of a home` WITH
            `the amount is to be used for the purchase of premises that the person intends to occupy as their home` IS `the amount is to be used to buy premises I intend to live in`
            `date on which the amount was received` IS `the day I received the amount`
            `the amount is attributable to the proceeds of sale of premises formerly occupied by the person as their home` IS `it comes from selling my former home`
            `the amount has been deposited with a housing association as mentioned in paragraph 12` IS `it has been deposited with a housing association`
            `the amount is a grant made to the person for the sole purpose of the purchase of a home` IS `it is a grant made only to buy a home`

-- Sch 10 para 14. An amount received under an insurance policy within the past 6 months in connection with the loss of or damage to your home or
-- your personal possessions is disregarded.
@export Is an insurance payout for my home or belongings disregarded (Sch 10 para 14)?
GIVEN `the amount was paid under an insurance policy for loss of or damage to my home or belongings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amount received under an insurance policy in connection with the loss of or damage to the premises occupied as your home or to your personal possessions?
      `the day I received the amount` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive it?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
      `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State extended the 6-month period in your case?
      `the months it has been extended to` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, to how many months? (0 if not extended)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an insurance payout for my home or belongings disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 14 — an amount received under an insurance policy` `the amount was paid under an insurance policy for loss of or damage to my home or belongings` `the day I received the amount` `the day my capital is being worked out` (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (IF `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` THEN JUST `the months it has been extended to` ELSE NOTHING))

-- Sch 10 para 15. An amount received within the past 6 months to be used for essential repairs or alterations to premises you occupy or intend to
-- occupy as your home is disregarded where you acquired it (by grant, loan or otherwise) on condition that it is used for that purpose.
@export Is an amount I received for essential repairs to my home disregarded (Sch 10 para 15)?
GIVEN `the amount is to be used for essential repairs or alterations to my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount to be used for making essential repairs or alterations to premises occupied or intended to be occupied as your home?
      `I got it on condition that it is used for that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire it (by grant, loan or otherwise) on condition that it is used for that purpose?
      `the day I received the amount` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive it?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
      `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State extended the 6-month period in your case?
      `the months it has been extended to` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, to how many months? (0 if not extended)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an amount I received for essential repairs to my home disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 15 — an amount for essential repairs or alterations` `the amount is to be used for essential repairs or alterations to my home` `I got it on condition that it is used for that` `the day I received the amount` `the day my capital is being worked out` (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (IF `the Secretary of State has extended the 6 months` THEN JUST `the months it has been extended to` ELSE NOTHING))


§§ `Other payments`

-- Sch 10 para 16. A payment made within the past 12 months under Part 8 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (the social fund) is disregarded.
@export Is a social fund payment I received disregarded (Sch 10 para 16)?
GIVEN `the payment was made under the social fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment made under Part 8 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (the social fund)?
      `the day the payment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the payment made?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a social fund payment I received disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 16 — a social fund payment` `the payment was made under the social fund` `the day the payment was made` `the day my capital is being worked out`

-- Sch 10 para 17. A payment made within the past 12 months by or on behalf of a local authority under one of the listed children's and social
-- services sections, or under any other enactment to meet your welfare needs related to old age or disability, other than living expenses (food,
-- ordinary clothing or footwear, household fuel, rent or other housing costs, for you, your partner or a child), is disregarded.
@export Is a payment I received from a local authority disregarded (Sch 10 para 17)?
GIVEN `the day the council paid it` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the payment made?
      `the body is in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is the body?
      `the body is` IS A `Kind of council` @desc What kind of body is it?
      `it was paid under one of the listed children's or social services sections` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made under section 17, 23B, 23C or 24A of the Children Act 1989, section 12 of the Social Work (Scotland) Act 1968, section 29 or 30 of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 or section 37, 38, 109, 110, 114 or 115 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014?
      `the provision is an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the Senedd` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was made under some other provision: is that provision an enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales?
      `the provision is an instrument under such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that provision an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales?
      `the provision is an enactment in some other way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that provision an enactment apart from those?
      `it is for my welfare needs related to old age or disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made in order to meet your welfare needs related to old age or disability?
      `it pays for food` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the cost of food?
      `it pays for ordinary clothing or footwear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the cost of ordinary clothing or footwear?
      `it pays for household fuel, rent or other housing costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the cost of household fuel, rent or other housing costs (including council tax)?
      `it is for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for you?
      `it is for my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for your partner?
      `it is for a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for a child or qualifying young person for whom you are responsible?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a payment I received from a local authority disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 17 — a payment by or on behalf of a local authority` `the council payment` `the day my capital is being worked out`
    WHERE
        `the council payment` MEANS `Payment by or on behalf of a local authority` WITH
            `date on which the payment was made` IS `the day the council paid it`
            `body` IS `the body that paid`
            `payment made under section 17, 23B, 23C or 24A of the Children Act 1989, section 12 of the Social Work (Scotland) Act 1968, section 29 or 30 of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 or section 37, 38, 109, 110, 114 or 115 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` IS `it was paid under one of the listed children's or social services sections`
            `provision` IS `the provision it was paid under`
            `payment made in order to meet a person's welfare needs related to old age or disability` IS `it is for my welfare needs related to old age or disability`
            `cost` IS `the cost it pays for`
        `the body that paid` MEANS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
            `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS `the body is in`
            `kind of body` IS `the body is`
        `the provision it was paid under` MEANS `Provision whose standing as an enactment is asked by uc2` WITH
            `enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales` IS `the provision is an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the Senedd`
            `instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales` IS `the provision is an instrument under such an Act`
            `an enactment apart from the inclusions in regulation 2` IS `the provision is an enactment in some other way`
        `the cost it pays for` MEANS `Cost that may be a living expense` WITH
            `cost of food` IS `it pays for food`
            `cost of ordinary clothing or footwear` IS `it pays for ordinary clothing or footwear`
            `cost of household fuel, rent or other housing costs (including council tax)` IS `it pays for household fuel, rent or other housing costs`
            `for the person` IS `it is for me`
            `for the person's partner` IS `it is for my partner`
            `for a child or qualifying young person for whom the person is responsible` IS `it is for a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`

-- Sch 10 para 18(2). A "social security benefit" is a benefit under any enactment relating to social security in any part of the United Kingdom,
-- and includes armed forces independence payment under the 2011 Order.
@export Is this benefit a social security benefit (Sch 10 para 18(2))?
GIVEN `it is a benefit under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a benefit under an enactment?
      `the provision is an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the Senedd` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales?
      `the provision is an instrument under such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales?
      `the provision is an enactment in some other way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an enactment apart from those?
      `the enactment relates to social security in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an enactment relating to social security in any part of the United Kingdom?
      `it is armed forces independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this benefit a social security benefit` IF
    `Sch 10 para 18(2) — social security benefit` `the benefit`
    WHERE
        `the benefit` MEANS `Payment that may be a social security benefit` WITH
            `benefit under an enactment` IS `it is a benefit under an enactment`
            `provision` IS `the benefit enactment`
            `enactment relating to social security in any part of the United Kingdom` IS `the enactment relates to social security in the United Kingdom`
            `armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011` IS `it is armed forces independence payment`
        `the benefit enactment` MEANS `Provision whose standing as an enactment is asked by uc2` WITH
            `enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales` IS `the provision is an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the Senedd`
            `instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales` IS `the provision is an instrument under such an Act`
            `an enactment apart from the inclusions in regulation 2` IS `the provision is an enactment in some other way`

-- Sch 10 para 18(1). A payment received within the past 12 months by way of arrears of, or compensation for late payment of, universal credit, a benefit
-- abolished by section 33 of the Act, or a social security benefit that is not included as unearned income under regulation 66(1)(a) or (b), is disregarded.
@export Are arrears of benefit I received disregarded (Sch 10 para 18(1))?
GIVEN `the payment is arrears of a benefit or compensation for late payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment by way of arrears of, or compensation for late payment of, a benefit?
      `the benefit is universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit universal credit?
      `the benefit is one abolished by section 33 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a benefit abolished by section 33 of the Act?
      `it is a benefit under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a benefit under an enactment?
      `the provision is an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the Senedd` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales?
      `the provision is an instrument under such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales?
      `the provision is an enactment in some other way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an enactment apart from those?
      `the enactment relates to social security in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an enactment relating to social security in any part of the United Kingdom?
      `it is armed forces independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011?
      `that benefit counts as my unearned income under regulation 66(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that benefit included as your unearned income under regulation 66(1)(a) or (b)?
      `the day I received the payment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the payment?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are arrears of benefit I received disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 18(1) — arrears of, or compensation for late payment of, a benefit` `the payment is arrears of a benefit or compensation for late payment` `the benefit is universal credit` `the benefit is one abolished by section 33 of the Act` `the benefit` `that benefit counts as my unearned income under regulation 66(1)(a) or (b)` `the day I received the payment` `the day my capital is being worked out`
    WHERE
        `the benefit` MEANS `Payment that may be a social security benefit` WITH
            `benefit under an enactment` IS `it is a benefit under an enactment`
            `provision` IS `the benefit enactment`
            `enactment relating to social security in any part of the United Kingdom` IS `the enactment relates to social security in the United Kingdom`
            `armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011` IS `it is armed forces independence payment`
        `the benefit enactment` MEANS `Provision whose standing as an enactment is asked by uc2` WITH
            `enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales` IS `the provision is an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the Senedd`
            `instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales` IS `the provision is an instrument under such an Act`
            `an enactment apart from the inclusions in regulation 2` IS `the provision is an enactment in some other way`

-- Sch 10 para 18ZA. A payment made within the past 12 months of widowed parent's allowance to the survivor of a cohabiting partnership who is entitled
-- to it for a period before the Bereavement Benefits (Remedial) Order 2023 comes into force, in respect of a period before the claim, is disregarded.
@export Is a payment of widowed parent's allowance I received disregarded (Sch 10 para 18ZA)?
GIVEN `the payment is widowed parent's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment a payment of widowed parent's allowance?
      `the day the payment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the payment made?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
      `I am the survivor of a cohabiting partnership entitled for a period before the 2023 Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the survivor of a cohabiting partnership who is entitled to widowed parent's allowance for a period before the Bereavement Benefits (Remedial) Order 2023 comes into force?
      `it is for a period before I made the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment in respect of a period ending with the day before you made the claim for widowed parent's allowance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a payment of widowed parent's allowance I received disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 18ZA — a payment of widowed parent's allowance to the survivor of a cohabiting partnership` `the payment is widowed parent's allowance` `the day the payment was made` `the day my capital is being worked out` `I am the survivor of a cohabiting partnership entitled for a period before the 2023 Order` `it is for a period before I made the claim`

-- Sch 10 para 18ZB. A payment to you made by the Secretary of State as a result of a recalculation of carer's allowance, carried out in consequence of the
-- report of the Independent Review of Carer's Allowance Overpayments dated 21st July 2025, is disregarded.
@export Is a payment I received on a recalculation of my carer's allowance disregarded (Sch 10 para 18ZB)?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State made the payment to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment made to you by the Secretary of State?
      `it follows the Independent Review of Carer's Allowance Overpayments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made as a result of a recalculation of carer's allowance carried out in consequence of the report of the Independent Review of Carer's Allowance Overpayments dated 21st July 2025?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a payment I received on a recalculation of my carer's allowance disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 18ZB — a payment on the recalculation of carer's allowance` `the Secretary of State made the payment to me` `it follows the Independent Review of Carer's Allowance Overpayments`

-- Sch 10 para 18A. A payment received within the past 12 months by way of local welfare provision, including arrears and payments in lieu of it, is disregarded.
@export Is a local welfare payment I received disregarded (Sch 10 para 18A)?
GIVEN `who gave the assistance` IS A `Giver of assistance` @desc Who gave the assistance?
      `it is occasional financial or other assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it occasional financial or other assistance?
      `it meets an immediate short term need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its purpose to meet, or help to meet, an immediate short term need?
      `the need arose from an exceptional event or circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the need arise out of an exceptional event, or exceptional circumstances?
      `it must be met to avoid a risk to someone's well-being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the need require to be met in order to avoid a risk to the well-being of an individual?
      `it is to help people establish or keep a settled home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its purpose enabling individuals to establish or maintain a settled home?
      `the people have been or might otherwise be in prison, hospital, a care home or other institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the individuals been, or might they otherwise be, in prison, hospital, a residential care establishment or other institution?
      `the people have been or might otherwise be homeless or living an unsettled way of life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the individuals been, or might they otherwise be, homeless or otherwise living an unsettled way of life?
      `it is arrears of local welfare provision or a payment in lieu of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment arrears of local welfare provision, or a payment in lieu of it?
      `the day I received the payment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the payment?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a local welfare payment I received disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 18A — a payment by way of local welfare provision` `the assistance` `it is arrears of local welfare provision or a payment in lieu of it` `the day I received the payment` `the day my capital is being worked out`
    WHERE
        `the assistance` MEANS `Assistance given to individuals` WITH
            `giver` IS `who gave the assistance`
            `assistance is occasional financial or other assistance` IS `it is occasional financial or other assistance`
            `purpose is meeting, or helping to meet, an immediate short term need` IS `it meets an immediate short term need`
            `need arises out of an exceptional event, or exceptional circumstances` IS `the need arose from an exceptional event or circumstances`
            `need requires to be met in order to avoid a risk to the well-being of an individual` IS `it must be met to avoid a risk to someone's well-being`
            `purpose is enabling individuals to establish or maintain a settled home` IS `it is to help people establish or keep a settled home`
            `individuals have been or, without the assistance, might otherwise be in prison, hospital, a residential care establishment or other institution` IS `the people have been or might otherwise be in prison, hospital, a care home or other institution`
            `individuals have been or, without the assistance, might otherwise be homeless or otherwise living an unsettled way of life` IS `the people have been or might otherwise be homeless or living an unsettled way of life`

-- Sch 10 para 19. A payment to you by virtue of being a holder of the Victoria Cross or George Cross is disregarded.
@export Is a payment I receive as a holder of the Victoria Cross or George Cross disregarded (Sch 10 para 19)?
GIVEN `the payment is made to me as a holder of the Victoria Cross or George Cross` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made to you by virtue of being a holder of the Victoria Cross or the George Cross?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a payment I receive as a holder of the Victoria Cross or George Cross disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 19 — a payment to a holder of the Victoria Cross or the George Cross` `the payment is made to me as a holder of the Victoria Cross or George Cross`

-- Sch 10 para 20(1). A payment made within the past 12 months of bereavement support payment at the rate in regulation 3(2) or (5) of the Bereavement
-- Support Payment Regulations 2017 is disregarded.
@export Is a bereavement support payment I received at the standard rate disregarded (Sch 10 para 20(1))?
GIVEN `the day the payment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the payment made?
      `it is at the rate in regulation 3(2) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment in respect of the rate set out in regulation 3(2) or (5) of the Bereavement Support Payment Regulations 2017?
      `I am the survivor of a cohabiting partnership whose partner died before the 2023 Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the survivor of a cohabiting partnership, in respect of a death before the day the Bereavement Benefits (Remedial) Order 2023 comes into force?
      `the amount at the rate in regulation 3(1)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the payment, in pounds, is in respect of the rate set out in regulation 3(1) of the Bereavement Support Payment Regulations 2017?
      `the part of it paid as a lump sum for more than one monthly recurrence` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the payment, in pounds, is paid as a lump sum for more than one monthly recurrence of the day of the month on which your cohabiting partner died?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a bereavement support payment I received at the standard rate disregarded` IF
    `Sch 10 para 20(1) — a payment of bereavement support payment at the rate in regulation 3(2) or (5)` `my payment` `the day my capital is being worked out`
    WHERE
        `my payment` MEANS `Bereavement support payment` WITH
            `date on which the payment was made` IS `the day the payment was made`
            `payment in respect of the rate set out in regulation 3(2) or (5) of the Bereavement Support Payment Regulations 2017` IS `it is at the rate in regulation 3(2) or (5)`
            `paid to the survivor of a cohabiting partnership in respect of a death before the day the Bereavement Benefits (Remedial) Order 2023 comes into force` IS `I am the survivor of a cohabiting partnership whose partner died before the 2023 Order`
            `amount of the payment in respect of the rate set out in regulation 3(1) of the Bereavement Support Payment Regulations 2017` IS `the amount at the rate in regulation 3(1)`
            `amount of that payment paid as a lump sum for more than one monthly recurrence of the day of the month on which their cohabiting partner died` IS `the part of it paid as a lump sum for more than one monthly recurrence`

-- Sch 10 para 20(2). Where bereavement support payment has been paid within the past 12 months to the survivor of a cohabiting partnership in respect of a
-- death before the 2023 Order comes into force, any amount of it that is in respect of the rate in regulation 3(1) and paid as a lump sum for more than one
-- monthly recurrence is disregarded. The seat reads the amount as the smaller of the two amounts you state (fork F-S10-4 in NOTES.md).
@export How much of my bereavement support payment is disregarded, in pounds (Sch 10 para 20(2))?
GIVEN `the day the payment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the payment made?
      `it is at the rate in regulation 3(2) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment in respect of the rate set out in regulation 3(2) or (5) of the Bereavement Support Payment Regulations 2017?
      `I am the survivor of a cohabiting partnership whose partner died before the 2023 Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the survivor of a cohabiting partnership, in respect of a death before the day the Bereavement Benefits (Remedial) Order 2023 comes into force?
      `the amount at the rate in regulation 3(1)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the payment, in pounds, is in respect of the rate set out in regulation 3(1) of the Bereavement Support Payment Regulations 2017?
      `the part of it paid as a lump sum for more than one monthly recurrence` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the payment, in pounds, is paid as a lump sum for more than one monthly recurrence of the day of the month on which your cohabiting partner died?
      `the day my capital is being worked out` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your capital being calculated?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my bereavement support payment is disregarded` IS
    `Sch 10 para 20(2) — the amount of the payment that is disregarded` `my payment` `the day my capital is being worked out`
    WHERE
        `my payment` MEANS `Bereavement support payment` WITH
            `date on which the payment was made` IS `the day the payment was made`
            `payment in respect of the rate set out in regulation 3(2) or (5) of the Bereavement Support Payment Regulations 2017` IS `it is at the rate in regulation 3(2) or (5)`
            `paid to the survivor of a cohabiting partnership in respect of a death before the day the Bereavement Benefits (Remedial) Order 2023 comes into force` IS `I am the survivor of a cohabiting partnership whose partner died before the 2023 Order`
            `amount of the payment in respect of the rate set out in regulation 3(1) of the Bereavement Support Payment Regulations 2017` IS `the amount at the rate in regulation 3(1)`
            `amount of that payment paid as a lump sum for more than one monthly recurrence of the day of the month on which their cohabiting partner died` IS `the part of it paid as a lump sum for more than one monthly recurrence`

-- Sch 10 para 21. Any early years assistance given within the past 12 months in accordance with section 32 of the Social Security (Scotland) Act 2018 is disregarded.
